{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WVn15CG7chqPGbJXmnP1VZ","type":"tool_result","content":"529\t      \"id\": \"US-024\",\n530\t      \"title\": \"Course creation wizard — Stage 1 (Topic) + Stage 2 (Refinement structured form)\",\n531\t      \"description\": \"As a learner starting a new course, I want to enter a topic and answer a few structured questions so the system has enough info to plan the course.\",\n532\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n533\t        \"Route /create is the wizard\",\n534\t        \"Step indicator at top (5 circles connected by 1px line, labels Topic / Refine / Structure / Approve / Generate); active = --accent filled, completed = --success check, future = outlined --border-strong; clicking a completed step jumps back to it\",\n535\t        \"Stage 1 (Topic): centered max-width 640px vertically centered; eyebrow 'What do you want to learn?' (--fs-sm --text-tertiary); big text input (--fs-2xl weight 500, --border underline only — no full border); placeholder cycles through 4 example topics every 3s; below input: 4 chip suggestions ('Backpropagation', 'Linear algebra for ML', 'How GPT works', 'Bayesian statistics') that pre-fill the input on click; 'Next' primary button right-aligned, enabled only when input has ≥3 words; pre-fills from ?topic=… query string when present (for Dashboard empty-state chips)\",\n536\t        \"Stage 2 (Refinement): centered max-width 720px; structured form (no LLM chat in MVP):  'What's your level?' 3 radio button cards (Beginner / Some experience / I know the basics);  'How long should this take?' 3 chip selectors (30 min / An hour / A weekend deep dive);  'Theory or practice?' slider 0–100 with label that updates live ('Mostly theory' / 'Balanced' / 'Mostly practice')\",\n537\t        \"Both stages persist draft to in-memory state (Zustand or React context); refresh resets state\",\n538\t        \"'Back' (ghost left) + 'Next' (primary right) footer; 'Back' from Stage 1 returns to dashboard with confirm dialog if input non-empty\",\n539\t        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: fill topic, click Next, fill refine form (level, duration, slider), click Next → lands on Stage 3 placeholder\",\n540\t        \"Typecheck passes\"\n541\t      ],\n542\t      \"priority\": 24,\n543\t      \"passes\": true,\n544\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n545\t      \"tags\": [\n546\t        \"ui\"\n547\t      ]\n548\t    },\n549\t    {\n550\t      \"id\": \"US-025\",\n551\t      \"title\": \"Course creation wizard — Stage 3 (Structure cascade)\",\n552\t      \"description\": \"As a learner, I want to see a draft course structure (modules + lessons) and edit it before generation so I can shape what the agent produces.\",\n553\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n554\t        \"Stage 3: 3-column cascade layout — Course | Modules | Lessons\",\n555\t        \"Column 1 (Course): single card showing course title (inline-editable) + 1-line description (inline-editable)\",\n556\t        \"Column 2 (Modules): list of 3-5 module cards seeded with placeholder defaults derived from the topic + level (simple template: 'Module 1: Intro to <topic>', 'Module 2: Core concepts', etc.); each card click selects → highlights + updates Column 3\",\n557\t        \"Drag-to-reorder modules (use @dnd-kit/sortable); '+' button at end of list to add a new module; trash icon on each card to remove (with inline confirm)\",\n558\t        \"Inline rename: click title to edit, blur or Enter to save\",\n559\t        \"Column 3 (Lessons of selected module): list of 4–8 lesson rows (title + 1-line description + estimated minutes); drag-to-reorder, inline rename, +/trash; defaults seeded similarly\",\n560\t        \"All edits persist into the in-memory draft (which becomes course-spec.json on Stage 5)\",\n561\t        \"Sticky bottom bar: 'Back' (ghost) | 'Looks good — generate' (primary) → advances to Stage 4\",\n562\t        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: reorder modules via drag-and-drop, rename a lesson, advance to Stage 4, confirm Stage 4 shows updated structure\",\n563\t        \"Typecheck passes\"\n564\t      ],\n565\t      \"priority\": 25,\n566\t      \"passes\": true,\n567\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n568\t      \"tags\": [\n569\t        \"ui\"\n570\t      ]\n571\t    },\n572\t    {\n573\t      \"id\": \"US-026\",\n574\t      \"title\": \"Course creation wizard — Stage 4 (Approval) + Stage 5 (Export to course-spec.json)\",\n575\t      \"description\": \"As a learner, I want to review the full course outline and get a clear command to run for generation, so the workflow from spec to generated lessons is unambiguous.\",\n576\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n577\t        \"Stage 4 (Approval): read-only summary of full outline rendered as a clean document — course title + description, then per module: module title, list of lessons with descriptions + estimated minutes, total time estimate; cost-estimate line ('≈ X minutes to generate, Y lessons' computed as lessonCount * 3min as a rough placeholder); big 'Generate course' primary button at bottom\",\n578\t        \"Stage 5 (Export): on click 'Generate course', POST /api/courses with the in-memory draft serialized as CourseSpec; API writes /courses/<slug>/course-spec.json (slug derived via slugify from courseTitle); on 409 (slug collision) prompts user to pick a different title\",\n579\t        \"Stage 5 view: success card with — (a) confirmation 'Course spec saved to /courses/<slug>/course-spec.json'; (b) monospace command block showing the next step: `claude` then invoke `init_course` skill with arg `<slug>` then `./scripts/ralph/ralph.sh`; with 'Copy' button per command; (c) friendly note 'The course will appear on your dashboard once generation completes'; (d) 'Back to dashboard' link\",\n580\t        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: walk through wizard end-to-end (Stage 1 → 2 → 3 → 4 → 5), confirm course-spec.json exists at expected path with expected contents (read file post-test and compare to schema)\",\n581\t        \"Typecheck passes\"\n582\t      ],\n583\t      \"priority\": 26,\n584\t      \"passes\": true,\n585\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n586\t      \"tags\": [\n587\t        \"ui\"\n588\t      ]\n589\t    },\n590\t    {\n591\t      \"id\": \"US-027\",\n592\t      \"title\": \"Ralph skill: init_course (course-spec → course-prd with research + per-lesson stories)\",\n593\t      \"description\": \"As an agent invoked by the user via Claude Code CLI, I want a SKILL.md that tells me how to convert a course-spec.json into a fresh course-prd.json with research + architect + per-lesson stories so ralph loop can iterate the course generation in separate, focused contexts.\",\n594\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n595\t        \"File: scripts/ralph/skills/init_course/SKILL.md\",\n596\t        \"Frontmatter: name: init_course, user-invocable: true, description triggers on phrases like 'init course', 'generate course from spec', 'create course prd', 'wygeneruj kurs', 'ralph init course'\",\n597\t        \"Skill expects argument: course slug (e.g. 'gauss-basics'); reads /courses/<slug>/course-spec.json, validates it against CourseSpecSchema\",\n598\t        \"Step 1 — Archive existing scripts/ralph/prd.json: if present and branchName differs from `ralph/course-<slug>`, copy current prd.json + progress.txt to scripts/ralph/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<old-branchName>/ and reset progress.txt with fresh header\",\n599\t        \"Step 2 — Research pass: synthesize key concepts, prerequisites, common misconceptions, suggested ordering for the topic; write to /courses/<slug>/research.md\",\n600\t        \"Step 3 — Architect pass: refine course-spec.draftStructure into final modules + lessons (may merge / split / rename / reorder), write /courses/<slug>/course.json validated against CourseSchema\",\n601\t        \"Step 4 — Generate course-prd.json with stories: US-001 'Compile research notes for course <title>' (output research.md), US-002 'Finalize course structure' (output course.json), US-003..N one per lesson 'Generate lesson: <lesson title>' (output /courses/<slug>/lessons/<lesson-slug>.json) with notes field carrying lesson summary + scope + level context, optional final story 'Review pass: validate all lessons against schema and fix issues'\",\n602\t        \"Each per-lesson story acceptanceCriteria includes: 'Lesson JSON validates against LessonSchema', 'Uses ≥3 widget types where the topic permits', 'Uses generate_lesson skill', 'Typecheck passes' (symbolic — story changes JSON not TS, but kept for ralph's standard validation)\",\n603\t        \"branchName for the new prd.json: `ralph/course-<slug>`\",\n604\t        \"SKILL.md instructs the agent to invoke generate_lesson skill when picking up per-lesson stories\",\n605\t        \"SKILL.md includes a worked example: input course-spec for 'edge-detection-basics', output prd.json structure with research + 4 lessons\",\n606\t        \"SKILL.md follows the same Step/Checklist pattern as scripts/ralph/skills/prd_init/SKILL.md (use it as a template)\",\n607\t        \"Manual smoke test: drop a sample course-spec.json into a test directory, run skill mentally (or live with claude), confirm prd.json structure matches schema\",\n608\t        \"Typecheck passes\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9bf3d4c0-be72-4235-a7a7-0162ef2f8d69","uuid":"9f24145e-3863-4878-b29e-f11101ebb584","timestamp":"2026-05-04T07:08:29.467Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/nukeemann/projects/ai_lecturer/.worktrees/US-056/scripts/ralph/prd.json","content":"      \"id\": \"US-024\",\n      \"title\": \"Course creation wizard — Stage 1 (Topic) + Stage 2 (Refinement structured form)\",\n      \"description\": \"As a learner starting a new course, I want to enter a topic and answer a few structured questions so the system has enough info to plan the course.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Route /create is the wizard\",\n        \"Step indicator at top (5 circles connected by 1px line, labels Topic / Refine / Structure / Approve / Generate); active = --accent filled, completed = --success check, future = outlined --border-strong; clicking a completed step jumps back to it\",\n        \"Stage 1 (Topic): centered max-width 640px vertically centered; eyebrow 'What do you want to learn?' (--fs-sm --text-tertiary); big text input (--fs-2xl weight 500, --border underline only — no full border); placeholder cycles through 4 example topics every 3s; below input: 4 chip suggestions ('Backpropagation', 'Linear algebra for ML', 'How GPT works', 'Bayesian statistics') that pre-fill the input on click; 'Next' primary button right-aligned, enabled only when input has ≥3 words; pre-fills from ?topic=… query string when present (for Dashboard empty-state chips)\",\n        \"Stage 2 (Refinement): centered max-width 720px; structured form (no LLM chat in MVP):  'What's your level?' 3 radio button cards (Beginner / Some experience / I know the basics);  'How long should this take?' 3 chip selectors (30 min / An hour / A weekend deep dive);  'Theory or practice?' slider 0–100 with label that updates live ('Mostly theory' / 'Balanced' / 'Mostly practice')\",\n        \"Both stages persist draft to in-memory state (Zustand or React context); refresh resets state\",\n        \"'Back' (ghost left) + 'Next' (primary right) footer; 'Back' from Stage 1 returns to dashboard with confirm dialog if input non-empty\",\n        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: fill topic, click Next, fill refine form (level, duration, slider), click Next → lands on Stage 3 placeholder\",\n        \"Typecheck passes\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 24,\n      \"passes\": true,\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"ui\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-025\",\n      \"title\": \"Course creation wizard — Stage 3 (Structure cascade)\",\n      \"description\": \"As a learner, I want to see a draft course structure (modules + lessons) and edit it before generation so I can shape what the agent produces.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Stage 3: 3-column cascade layout — Course | Modules | Lessons\",\n        \"Column 1 (Course): single card showing course title (inline-editable) + 1-line description (inline-editable)\",\n        \"Column 2 (Modules): list of 3-5 module cards seeded with placeholder defaults derived from the topic + level (simple template: 'Module 1: Intro to <topic>', 'Module 2: Core concepts', etc.); each card click selects → highlights + updates Column 3\",\n        \"Drag-to-reorder modules (use @dnd-kit/sortable); '+' button at end of list to add a new module; trash icon on each card to remove (with inline confirm)\",\n        \"Inline rename: click title to edit, blur or Enter to save\",\n        \"Column 3 (Lessons of selected module): list of 4–8 lesson rows (title + 1-line description + estimated minutes); drag-to-reorder, inline rename, +/trash; defaults seeded similarly\",\n        \"All edits persist into the in-memory draft (which becomes course-spec.json on Stage 5)\",\n        \"Sticky bottom bar: 'Back' (ghost) | 'Looks good — generate' (primary) → advances to Stage 4\",\n        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: reorder modules via drag-and-drop, rename a lesson, advance to Stage 4, confirm Stage 4 shows updated structure\",\n        \"Typecheck passes\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 25,\n      \"passes\": true,\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"ui\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-026\",\n      \"title\": \"Course creation wizard — Stage 4 (Approval) + Stage 5 (Export to course-spec.json)\",\n      \"description\": \"As a learner, I want to review the full course outline and get a clear command to run for generation, so the workflow from spec to generated lessons is unambiguous.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Stage 4 (Approval): read-only summary of full outline rendered as a clean document — course title + description, then per module: module title, list of lessons with descriptions + estimated minutes, total time estimate; cost-estimate line ('≈ X minutes to generate, Y lessons' computed as lessonCount * 3min as a rough placeholder); big 'Generate course' primary button at bottom\",\n        \"Stage 5 (Export): on click 'Generate course', POST /api/courses with the in-memory draft serialized as CourseSpec; API writes /courses/<slug>/course-spec.json (slug derived via slugify from courseTitle); on 409 (slug collision) prompts user to pick a different title\",\n        \"Stage 5 view: success card with — (a) confirmation 'Course spec saved to /courses/<slug>/course-spec.json'; (b) monospace command block showing the next step: `claude` then invoke `init_course` skill with arg `<slug>` then `./scripts/ralph/ralph.sh`; with 'Copy' button per command; (c) friendly note 'The course will appear on your dashboard once generation completes'; (d) 'Back to dashboard' link\",\n        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: walk through wizard end-to-end (Stage 1 → 2 → 3 → 4 → 5), confirm course-spec.json exists at expected path with expected contents (read file post-test and compare to schema)\",\n        \"Typecheck passes\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 26,\n      \"passes\": true,\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"ui\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-027\",\n      \"title\": \"Ralph skill: init_course (course-spec → course-prd with research + per-lesson stories)\",\n      \"description\": \"As an agent invoked by the user via Claude Code CLI, I want a SKILL.md that tells me how to convert a course-spec.json into a fresh course-prd.json with research + architect + per-lesson stories so ralph loop can iterate the course generation in separate, focused contexts.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"File: scripts/ralph/skills/init_course/SKILL.md\",\n        \"Frontmatter: name: init_course, user-invocable: true, description triggers on phrases like 'init course', 'generate course from spec', 'create course prd', 'wygeneruj kurs', 'ralph init course'\",\n        \"Skill expects argument: course slug (e.g. 'gauss-basics'); reads /courses/<slug>/course-spec.json, validates it against CourseSpecSchema\",\n        \"Step 1 — Archive existing scripts/ralph/prd.json: if present and branchName differs from `ralph/course-<slug>`, copy current prd.json + progress.txt to scripts/ralph/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<old-branchName>/ and reset progress.txt with fresh header\",\n        \"Step 2 — Research pass: synthesize key concepts, prerequisites, common misconceptions, suggested ordering for the topic; write to /courses/<slug>/research.md\",\n        \"Step 3 — Architect pass: refine course-spec.draftStructure into final modules + lessons (may merge / split / rename / reorder), write /courses/<slug>/course.json validated against CourseSchema\",\n        \"Step 4 — Generate course-prd.json with stories: US-001 'Compile research notes for course <title>' (output research.md), US-002 'Finalize course structure' (output course.json), US-003..N one per lesson 'Generate lesson: <lesson title>' (output /courses/<slug>/lessons/<lesson-slug>.json) with notes field carrying lesson summary + scope + level context, optional final story 'Review pass: validate all lessons against schema and fix issues'\",\n        \"Each per-lesson story acceptanceCriteria includes: 'Lesson JSON validates against LessonSchema', 'Uses ≥3 widget types where the topic permits', 'Uses generate_lesson skill', 'Typecheck passes' (symbolic — story changes JSON not TS, but kept for ralph's standard validation)\",\n        \"branchName for the new prd.json: `ralph/course-<slug>`\",\n        \"SKILL.md instructs the agent to invoke generate_lesson skill when picking up per-lesson stories\",\n        \"SKILL.md includes a worked example: input course-spec for 'edge-detection-basics', output prd.json structure with research + 4 lessons\",\n        \"SKILL.md follows the same Step/Checklist pattern as scripts/ralph/skills/prd_init/SKILL.md (use it as a template)\",\n        \"Manual smoke test: drop a sample course-spec.json into a test directory, run skill mentally (or live with claude), confirm prd.json structure matches schema\",\n        \"Typecheck passes\"","numLines":80,"startLine":529,"totalLines":1307}}}
