{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Suf163rL8TfDX4aXTHp28z","type":"tool_result","content":"780\t      \"id\": \"US-036\",\n781\t      \"title\": \"Search bar functional — title/description/theory content with <slug>: autocomplete\",\n782\t      \"description\": \"As a user with multiple courses, I want the dashboard search bar to filter courses by title, description, and theory content (markdown only — not widget data like quiz/code), with a `<slug>:` prefix to scope searches into a single course.\",\n783\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n784\t        \"Dashboard search input (existing decorative input from US-014) wires to live filtering\",\n785\t        \"Search index built client-side on dashboard mount: { courseSlug, courseTitle, courseDescription, theoryContent: concatenated markdown of all theory sections across all lessons in the course } — quiz/code/demo/sandbox data NOT indexed\",\n786\t        \"Default mode (no `<slug>:` prefix): substring match (case-insensitive) against title + description + theoryContent of all courses; matching courses shown in grid, non-matching hidden; 'No courses match' empty state when nothing matches\",\n787\t        \"Slug-prefix mode: typing `<slug>:` (e.g. `gauss-basics:`) restricts search to that course's content; matching shown as result list under the input with lesson title + snippet (≤120 chars around match) + click navigates to /courses/<slug>/lessons/<lesson-slug>\",\n788\t        \"Autocomplete: while typing slug name (before colon), show dropdown of matching course slugs as suggestions; selecting one fills `<slug>:` into input and focuses cursor after the colon\",\n789\t        \"Empty input restores full grid (no filtering)\",\n790\t        \"Debounce input 150ms; case-insensitive throughout; accent-stripping for Polish characters welcome but not required\",\n791\t        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: with seed gauss-basics course, type 'gauss', confirm card visible; type 'nonsense', confirm grid empty + 'no matches' state; type 'gauss-b', see autocomplete suggesting gauss-basics; type 'gauss-basics: kernel', see results from theory containing 'kernel'\",\n792\t        \"Typecheck passes\",\n793\t        \"Tests pass\"\n794\t      ],\n795\t      \"priority\": 36,\n796\t      \"passes\": true,\n797\t      \"notes\": \"Widget content (quiz questions, code task descriptions, demo params) explicitly excluded from index per user decision.\",\n798\t      \"tags\": [\n799\t        \"ui\"\n800\t      ]\n801\t    },\n802\t    {\n803\t      \"id\": \"US-037\",\n804\t      \"title\": \"Add schemaVersion field to Course and Lesson schemas (forward-compat only)\",\n805\t      \"description\": \"As a developer maintaining the app long-term, I want a schemaVersion field on Course and Lesson JSON so future schema migrations have a known baseline; no migration logic in MVP — field only.\",\n806\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n807\t        \"CourseSchema in src/lib/schemas/course.ts gains `schemaVersion: number` field, default 1; missing field on parse defaults to 1\",\n808\t        \"LessonSchema in src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts gains `schemaVersion: number` field, default 1; missing field on parse defaults to 1\",\n809\t        \"init_course skill writes schemaVersion: 1 in generated course.json\",\n810\t        \"generate_lesson skill writes schemaVersion: 1 in generated lesson JSON\",\n811\t        \"Existing seed course gauss-basics course.json + both lessons updated to include schemaVersion: 1\",\n812\t        \"JSON Schemas regenerated via `npm run build:schemas`; schemaVersion appears in src/widgets/schemas/course.json and lesson.json\",\n813\t        \"Vitest tests cover: parse succeeds when schemaVersion missing (defaults to 1); parse succeeds when schemaVersion: 1 present\",\n814\t        \"Typecheck passes\",\n815\t        \"Tests pass\"\n816\t      ],\n817\t      \"priority\": 37,\n818\t      \"passes\": true,\n819\t      \"notes\": \"Forward-compat field only — no migration logic in MVP per user decision.\",\n820\t      \"tags\": []\n821\t    },\n822\t    {\n823\t      \"id\": \"US-038\",\n824\t      \"title\": \"Peek solution button in Code widget — always available, no confirm\",\n825\t      \"description\": \"As a learner stuck on a code exercise, I want a 'Peek solution' button always available that reveals the reference solution in a read-only block, so I can unblock myself without confirmation friction.\",\n826\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n827\t        \"CodeData schema in src/widgets/Code/schema.ts gains optional field `solution?: string` (Python source); zod-to-json-schema regenerates code.json\",\n828\t        \"Code Exercise widget footer adds a 'Peek solution' ghost button when `solution` field is present in section data; button absent when no solution defined\",\n829\t        \"Click 'Peek solution' → expands an inline read-only CodeMirror block (Python syntax-highlighted, --bg-subtle bg, 1px --border, --radius-md) below the test panel labeled 'Reference solution'; no modal, no confirm dialog\",\n830\t        \"Button label flips to 'Hide solution' while expanded; click again collapses\",\n831\t        \"Solution NOT auto-injected into editor — user must manually copy if they want to use it\",\n832\t        \"WidgetEditPanel for Code widget gains a 'Solution (optional)' CodeMirror Python field; saving persists into lesson JSON\",\n833\t        \"Solution panel renders BELOW test results so it doesn't compete for attention with the user's own attempt\",\n834\t        \"Seed course gauss-basics Lesson 2 code exercise (gauss_blur) updated to include a sample reference solution\",\n835\t        \"generate_lesson skill (SKILL.md) updated to instruct: populate `solution` field for every code exercise it generates\",\n836\t        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: load Code widget with solution defined, click 'Peek solution', confirm panel expands with solution code; click again, confirm collapses; load Code widget without solution, confirm button absent\",\n837\t        \"Typecheck passes\"\n838\t      ],\n839\t      \"priority\": 38,\n840\t      \"passes\": true,\n841\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n842\t      \"tags\": [\n843\t        \"ui\"\n844\t      ]\n845\t    },\n846\t    {\n847\t      \"id\": \"US-039\",\n848\t      \"title\": \"Stop running code — terminate Pyodide worker + restart with notice\",\n849\t      \"description\": \"As a learner who started a long-running or infinite-loop Python execution, I want a Stop button that terminates the worker and gives me a clear message so I can continue working without reloading the page.\",\n850\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n851\t        \"CodeRunner (US-010) Run button morphs into 'Stop' (--danger styling) while Pyodide execution is in flight; same morph in Sandbox, ParametricExplorer, PythonPlot widgets\",\n852\t        \"Click 'Stop' → calls worker.terminate() on the Pyodide Web Worker, spawns a fresh worker, marks pyodide status='loading' until new worker is ready\",\n853\t        \"After restart: lesson namespace from US-031 is cleared (new worker has no state); output panel shows a Callout (warning tone): 'Session restarted — re-run previous cells if needed.'\",\n854\t        \"Default execution timeout (30s) auto-triggers same termination + slightly different Callout: 'Execution timed out after 30s. Session restarted.'\",\n855\t        \"Restart re-installs matplotlib / numpy / scipy lazily on next use (singleton flags reset alongside worker)\",\n856\t        \"All Python-executing widgets in current lesson reflect the cleared-namespace state on next interaction\",\n857\t        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: type `while True: pass` in Sandbox, click Run, confirm Run button morphs to Stop; click Stop; confirm output shows 'Session restarted' Callout; then run `print(1+1)` and confirm it works without page reload\",\n858\t        \"Typecheck passes\",\n859\t        \"Tests pass\"\n860\t      ],\n861\t      \"priority\": 39,\n862\t      \"passes\": true,\n863\t      \"notes\": \"Pyodide does not support native Python interrupt; full worker termination is the only reliable path. User accepted the trade-off of losing namespace per option B.\",\n864\t      \"tags\": [\n865\t        \"ui\"\n866\t      ]\n867\t    },\n868\t    {\n869\t      \"id\": \"US-040\",\n870\t      \"title\": \"Sources/citations on Lesson + per-section — schema + render expandable panel\",\n871\t      \"description\": \"As a learner, I want each lesson to expose a clickable list of sources (papers, videos, articles, books) both at lesson-level (overall references) and at section-level (per-topic citations), so I can dig deeper into the material.\",\n872\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n873\t        \"LessonSchema gains `sources?: Array<{ url: string, title: string, kind: 'paper' | 'video' | 'article' | 'book', author?: string, year?: number }>` (lesson-level)\",\n874\t        \"SectionSchema base gains `sources?: Array<...same shape...>` (section-level, optional on every section type via the discriminated union)\",\n875\t        \"Lesson view bottom area (above bottom bar) renders a collapsible 'Źródła / Sources' section listing all lesson-level sources as clickable cards: icon per kind (paper=FileText, video=Video, article=Newspaper, book=BookOpen — lucide), title, author/year inline, URL displayed in --text-tertiary\",\n876\t        \"Each section widget header gets a small lucide Link icon (16px) next to the status badge when section.sources is non-empty; click opens a popover listing that section's sources\",\n877\t        \"Cards open URL in new tab (target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer')\",\n878\t        \"Editor (lesson-level): in lesson edit context (or via a 'Lesson sources' button in the lesson header), simple list with add/remove + url/title/kind/author/year fields; per-section sources editor folded into existing WidgetEditPanel as an optional 'Sources' section at bottom\",\n879\t        \"JSON Schemas regenerated via npm run build:schemas\",\n880\t        \"Seed course gauss-basics gets at least 3 lesson-level sources added (e.g. Wikipedia Gaussian filter, scikit-image docs, OpenCV tutorial)\",\n881\t        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: open seed lesson 2, expand sources section, confirm 3+ cards rendered with correct icons; click one and verify target='_blank'; check section-level icon on a section that has sources\",\n882\t        \"Typecheck passes\",\n883\t        \"Tests pass\"\n884\t      ],\n885\t      \"priority\": 40,\n886\t      \"passes\": true,\n887\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n888\t      \"tags\": [\n889\t        \"ui\"\n890\t      ]\n891\t    },\n892\t    {\n893\t      \"id\": \"US-041\",\n894\t      \"title\": \"Update generate_lesson + init_course skills — emphasize sources/publications/videos\",\n895\t      \"description\": \"As an agent generating lessons, I want explicit guidance to research and cite sources before writing content, so generated lessons include credible references in the new sources field from US-040.\",\n896\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n897\t        \"scripts/ralph/skills/generate_lesson/SKILL.md updated with new section 'Source Research' before generation rules\",\n898\t        \"Skill instructs: before generating content, perform a research pass to identify ≥3 credible sources (papers with DOI/arxiv, textbook chapters, reputable articles, recognized educational videos like 3Blue1Brown / StatQuest); record them\",\n899\t        \"Skill instructs: populate lesson-level `sources` field with ≥3 entries; populate section-level `sources` for theory sections that draw on a specific reference\",\n900\t        \"Skill instructs: prefer URLs that are stable (DOI, arxiv, official docs, Wikipedia for foundational concepts, official YouTube channels); avoid blog hosts likely to break (medium, towardsdatascience)\",\n901\t        \"Skill instructs: every source MUST have non-empty title; author + year strongly preferred for papers/books\",\n902\t        \"scripts/ralph/skills/init_course/SKILL.md updated: research step (Step 2) now explicitly produces a sources.md file alongside research.md, listing collected references; per-lesson stories in generated prd.json carry source hints in notes field so generate_lesson can pick them up\",\n903\t        \"Worked example in generate_lesson SKILL.md updated to show populated lesson-level sources (3+ entries) and one section-level source\",\n904\t        \"Worked example in init_course SKILL.md updated to show sources.md output\","}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9bf3d4c0-be72-4235-a7a7-0162ef2f8d69","uuid":"772e00eb-8fbc-48c8-a69b-db755853f3aa","timestamp":"2026-05-04T07:08:34.461Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/nukeemann/projects/ai_lecturer/.worktrees/US-056/scripts/ralph/prd.json","content":"      \"id\": \"US-036\",\n      \"title\": \"Search bar functional — title/description/theory content with <slug>: autocomplete\",\n      \"description\": \"As a user with multiple courses, I want the dashboard search bar to filter courses by title, description, and theory content (markdown only — not widget data like quiz/code), with a `<slug>:` prefix to scope searches into a single course.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Dashboard search input (existing decorative input from US-014) wires to live filtering\",\n        \"Search index built client-side on dashboard mount: { courseSlug, courseTitle, courseDescription, theoryContent: concatenated markdown of all theory sections across all lessons in the course } — quiz/code/demo/sandbox data NOT indexed\",\n        \"Default mode (no `<slug>:` prefix): substring match (case-insensitive) against title + description + theoryContent of all courses; matching courses shown in grid, non-matching hidden; 'No courses match' empty state when nothing matches\",\n        \"Slug-prefix mode: typing `<slug>:` (e.g. `gauss-basics:`) restricts search to that course's content; matching shown as result list under the input with lesson title + snippet (≤120 chars around match) + click navigates to /courses/<slug>/lessons/<lesson-slug>\",\n        \"Autocomplete: while typing slug name (before colon), show dropdown of matching course slugs as suggestions; selecting one fills `<slug>:` into input and focuses cursor after the colon\",\n        \"Empty input restores full grid (no filtering)\",\n        \"Debounce input 150ms; case-insensitive throughout; accent-stripping for Polish characters welcome but not required\",\n        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: with seed gauss-basics course, type 'gauss', confirm card visible; type 'nonsense', confirm grid empty + 'no matches' state; type 'gauss-b', see autocomplete suggesting gauss-basics; type 'gauss-basics: kernel', see results from theory containing 'kernel'\",\n        \"Typecheck passes\",\n        \"Tests pass\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 36,\n      \"passes\": true,\n      \"notes\": \"Widget content (quiz questions, code task descriptions, demo params) explicitly excluded from index per user decision.\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"ui\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-037\",\n      \"title\": \"Add schemaVersion field to Course and Lesson schemas (forward-compat only)\",\n      \"description\": \"As a developer maintaining the app long-term, I want a schemaVersion field on Course and Lesson JSON so future schema migrations have a known baseline; no migration logic in MVP — field only.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"CourseSchema in src/lib/schemas/course.ts gains `schemaVersion: number` field, default 1; missing field on parse defaults to 1\",\n        \"LessonSchema in src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts gains `schemaVersion: number` field, default 1; missing field on parse defaults to 1\",\n        \"init_course skill writes schemaVersion: 1 in generated course.json\",\n     