{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EkFhLg8sruRS6CSuAxeANE","type":"tool_result","content":"303\t      \"id\": \"US-014\",\n304\t      \"title\": \"Dashboard — course grid + Continue learning hero + New course CTA\",\n305\t      \"description\": \"As a learner, I want a home screen showing my courses and a clear way to create new ones so I know where to start each session.\",\n306\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n307\t        \"Route / is the dashboard\",\n308\t        \"Top header (64px): logo/app name left, search input centered (decorative placeholder for MVP — no behavior), theme toggle slot + settings icon + avatar right\",\n309\t        \"Max-width 1080px content area, padding var(--space-7) var(--space-6)\",\n310\t        \"'Continue learning' hero card visible only when at least one course has lastVisitedAt: full content-width, --radius-xl, --bg-elevated, 1px --border; left side has accent-tinted course icon + breadcrumb + lesson title (--fs-2xl weight 600); right side has big 'Resume' primary button → routes to /courses/[slug]/lessons/[lessonSlug]\",\n311\t        \"When no progress, hero is hidden (no stub)\",\n312\t        \"Course grid: CSS grid `repeat(auto-fill, minmax(320px, 1fr))`, gap var(--space-5)\",\n313\t        \"Each card: --bg-elevated, --radius-lg, 1px --border, padding var(--space-5); 36px round icon (color = course's accentColor from schema, lucide icon from course.icon); title (--fs-lg weight 600); 1-line description; status badge ('New' / 'In progress · X/Y' / 'Completed'); 4px progress bar at bottom\",\n314\t        \"Hover: border darkens to --border-strong + subtle --shadow-sm lift\",\n315\t        \"Empty state (when 0 courses): replace grid with centered 'Create your first course' card (--bg-elevated, --radius-xl, padding generous) + 4 starter topic chips ('Linear algebra basics', 'How transformers work', 'Computer vision basics', 'Bayesian statistics') — chips route to /create with topic prefilled via query string\",\n316\t        \"'+ Nowy kurs' primary button top-right of content area, routes to /create\",\n317\t        \"Dashboard re-fetches GET /api/courses + GET /api/progress on mount; refetch on window focus\",\n318\t        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: with 0 courses → empty state visible; with mock courses + progress → grid + hero render; click a card → navigates to lesson\",\n319\t        \"Typecheck passes\"\n320\t      ],\n321\t      \"priority\": 14,\n322\t      \"passes\": true,\n323\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n324\t      \"tags\": [\n325\t        \"ui\"\n326\t      ]\n327\t    },\n328\t    {\n329\t      \"id\": \"US-015\",\n330\t      \"title\": \"Lesson view shell — 3-col layout + toolbar + bottom bar placeholders\",\n331\t      \"description\": \"As a learner, I want a 3-column lesson layout with a top toolbar and bottom bar so the full notebook-style learning surface is in place for content + navigation.\",\n332\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n333\t        \"Route /courses/[slug]/lessons/[lessonSlug] renders the lesson shell\",\n334\t        \"CSS grid: grid-template-columns: <tocCol> minmax(0,1fr) <chatCol>, rows '52px 1fr 56px'; tocCol = 276px expanded / 52px collapsed; chatCol = 320px when chat open / 0 when closed (chat closed by default in MVP)\",\n335\t        \"Toolbar 52px: breadcrumb left ('Course › Module › Lesson', lesson name in --text, others --text-tertiary, --fs-sm, clickable), spacer flex-1, section progress pill (N/M mono in --bg-subtle 1px --border --radius-md padding 4px 10px) + 60×4px segmented progress bar, vertical 1px×22px --border divider, theme toggle slot, icon button '?' for shortcuts, icon button '⌘.' for tutor (disabled / greyed in MVP since tutor not implemented)\",\n336\t        \"Right column placeholder: empty <aside> with width 0 in MVP; when expanded, shows a single centered note 'AI tutor — coming soon'\",\n337\t        \"Bottom bar 56px: empty placeholder for prev/mark/next (filled in US-018)\",\n338\t        \"Center column: ready to host content stream from US-017\",\n339\t        \"Lesson data fetched from GET /api/courses/[slug]/lessons/[lessonSlug] on mount; loading state = skeleton bars (3 stacked bars matching widget heights) in content area; error state = Callout 'Lesson not found' with link back to course\",\n340\t        \"On lesson mount: PATCH /api/progress with { courseSlug, lessonSlug, status: 'started', markVisited: true } — but only update status if currently 'not_started' (don't downgrade 'finished' to 'started')\",\n341\t        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: navigate to a stub lesson, confirm 3-col layout + toolbar + bottom bar render in both light and dark\",\n342\t        \"Typecheck passes\"\n343\t      ],\n344\t      \"priority\": 15,\n345\t      \"passes\": true,\n346\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n347\t      \"tags\": [\n348\t        \"ui\"\n349\t      ]\n350\t    },\n351\t    {\n352\t      \"id\": \"US-016\",\n353\t      \"title\": \"TOC sidebar — modules, lessons, status dots, collapse\",\n354\t      \"description\": \"As a learner, I want a left sidebar listing all modules and lessons in this course with my progress status, so I can navigate at any time.\",\n355\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n356\t        \"Left column 276px expanded, 52px collapsed; toggle persists to localStorage['toc-collapsed']\",\n357\t        \"Header: 'All courses' eyebrow link (back to dashboard, --fs-xs uppercase letter-spacing 0.06em weight 600 --text-tertiary) above course title (--fs-sm weight 600)\",\n358\t        \"Each module is a collapsible group with header (--fs-sm weight 600) and chevron; click toggles expansion of its lessons\",\n359\t        \"Each lesson row: 28px tall, padding 0 12px, --fs-sm, gap-2 between status dot + label, label truncated with ellipsis on overflow\",\n360\t        \"Status dot 6px circle: --success solid (finished), --accent solid (started), --border-strong hollow ring (not_started); reads from progress\",\n361\t        \"Active lesson row: --accent-subtle bg, label color --accent-text, weight 600, 2px-wide left accent border bleeding into row\",\n362\t        \"Click on lesson row → router.push to that lesson\",\n363\t        \"Collapsed state (52px): only status dots visible vertically stacked; hover on dot → tooltip with lesson title\",\n364\t        \"180ms width transition on collapse/expand\",\n365\t        \"Toggle button (icon-only chevron) in TOC header right-side\",\n366\t        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: render lesson with course of 2 modules × 3 lessons, click another lesson → confirm navigation; toggle collapse → confirm width animation + tooltips on dots\",\n367\t        \"Typecheck passes\"\n368\t      ],\n369\t      \"priority\": 16,\n370\t      \"passes\": true,\n371\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n372\t      \"tags\": [\n373\t        \"ui\"\n374\t      ]\n375\t    },\n376\t    {\n377\t      \"id\": \"US-017\",\n378\t      \"title\": \"Content stream — lesson header + widgets in order\",\n379\t      \"description\": \"As a learner, I want the lesson content to flow as a vertical stack of typed widgets so each section is self-contained and the lesson reads like a notebook.\",\n380\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n381\t        \"Center column: vertical scroll, max-content-width 760px, centered, with --space-6 horizontal padding\",\n382\t        \"Lesson header above first widget: eyebrow 'Module N · Lesson M' (--fs-xs uppercase letter-spacing 0.06em weight 600 --text-tertiary), H1 lesson title (--fs-3xl weight 600 letter-spacing -0.02em), 1-line description (--text-secondary --fs-md)\",\n383\t        \"Section widgets stacked with var(--space-section) gaps; rendered by looking up section.type in widgetRegistry and rendering its component with section.data\",\n384\t        \"Each section gets id='section-<sectionId>' so TOC + scrollIntoView + URL hash navigation can target it\",\n385\t        \"Unknown widget type renders a fallback Callout 'Unsupported widget type: <type>' (warning tone)\",\n386\t        \"Section number (§N) auto-derived from index in lesson.sections[]\",\n387\t        \"Widget header status badge derived per section from progress.sectionState (if any) or from completion auto-detection (e.g. quiz answered correctly, code submitted passing)\",\n388\t        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: render a lesson stub with all 5 widget types in sequence, confirm all render with correct accent rails and spacing\",\n389\t        \"Typecheck passes\"\n390\t      ],\n391\t      \"priority\": 17,\n392\t      \"passes\": true,\n393\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n394\t      \"tags\": [\n395\t        \"ui\"\n396\t      ]\n397\t    },\n398\t    {\n399\t      \"id\": \"US-018\",\n400\t      \"title\": \"Bottom bar — prev / mark complete / next + auto-advance\",\n401\t      \"description\": \"As a learner, I want prev/next navigation and a Mark complete button at the bottom of every lesson so I can move through the course at my own pace.\",\n402\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n403\t        \"Bottom bar 56px filled per design\",\n404\t        \"Prev button (left, ghost): eyebrow 'Previous' + previous lesson title (truncated); disabled when first lesson in course; click → router.push to prev lesson\",\n405\t        \"Center: 'Mark lesson complete' button — primary if lesson status !== 'finished', otherwise rendered as 'Lesson completed' with check icon (ghost styling)\",\n406\t        \"Click on Mark complete → PATCH /api/progress with { status: 'finished' }, button morphs to 'Lesson completed'\",\n407\t        \"Next button (right, ghost): eyebrow 'Next' + next lesson title; disabled when last lesson; click → router.push to next lesson\",\n408\t        \"Auto-advance: when 'Mark complete' clicked AND a next lesson exists in this course, after 600ms fade-out animation, router.push to next lesson\",\n409\t        \"Prev/next resolution: walk course.modules → flatten to ordered list of lessons across all modules in display order, find current lesson index, prev = index-1 if exists, next = index+1 if exists\",\n410\t        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: navigate to middle lesson, click Mark complete, observe 600ms fade + auto-advance to next; confirm finished status persists\",\n411\t        \"Typecheck passes\"\n412\t      ],\n413\t      \"priority\": 18,\n414\t      \"passes\": true,\n415\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n416\t      \"tags\": [\n417\t        \"ui\"\n418\t      ]\n419\t    },\n420\t    {\n421\t      \"id\": \"US-019\",\n422\t      \"title\": \"Progress wiring — TOC dots + dashboard cards/hero stay in sync\",\n423\t      \"description\": \"As a learner, I want my progress (started/finished) reflected consistently in the TOC dots, dashboard cards, and Continue learning hero so the UI never lies about my state.\",\n424\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n425\t        \"All three surfaces (TOC, dashboard cards, dashboard hero) read the same GET /api/progress endpoint and reflect current status\",\n426\t        \"Course card status badge derived as: 0 lessons started → 'New'; any started but not all finished → 'In progress · X/Y' (X=finished count, Y=total lessons); all finished → 'Completed'\",\n427\t        \"Course card progress bar fill = finishedCount / totalLessons\",\n428\t        \"Continue learning hero on dashboard reads lastVisitedAt across all courses, picks the one with the latest timestamp, shows its lastVisitedLessonSlug\",\n429\t        \"When the user clicks Mark complete in lesson view (US-018) and returns to dashboard via prev navigation or 'All courses' link, dashboard reflects new status without manual refresh (refetch on focus is enough)\",\n430\t        \"TOC dots in lesson view live-update when current lesson is marked complete (no full reload required)\",\n431\t        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: complete one lesson, return to dashboard, confirm card badge changes to 'In progress · 1/N' and hero shows that course\",\n432\t        \"Typecheck passes\"\n433\t      ],\n434\t      \"priority\": 19,\n435\t      \"passes\": true,\n436\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n437\t      \"tags\": [\n438\t        \"ui\"\n439\t      ]\n440\t    },\n441\t    {\n442\t      \"id\": \"US-020\",\n443\t      \"title\": \"Theme toggle (light/dark) in dashboard header + lesson toolbar\",\n444\t      \"description\": \"As a learner, I want a sun/moon button in both the dashboard header and the lesson toolbar to switch between light and dark mode, with my choice remembered.\",\n445\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n446\t        \"<ThemeToggle /> component renders a 28px icon button: shows sun icon when current data-theme='dark' (clicking → switches to light), moon icon when current data-theme='light' (clicking → switches to dark)\",\n447\t        \"Click toggles <html data-theme> attribute and persists choice to localStorage['theme']\",\n448\t        \"On app boot: an inline blocking script in <head> reads localStorage['theme'] and applies before React hydrates (prevents FOUC); fallback: prefers-color-scheme when localStorage['theme'] unset\",\n449\t        \"Mounted in dashboard header (between settings and avatar) AND in lesson toolbar (between section progress pill and shortcuts button '?')\",\n450\t        \"120ms transition on icon swap (opacity + 180° rotate)\",\n451\t        \"Respects prefers-color-scheme on first load only; subsequent loads honor user's last manual choice\",\n452\t        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: load dashboard in light mode, click toggle, confirm CSS vars switch (background changes, all sample swatches recolor); reload page, confirm dark mode persisted; same flow inside a lesson view\",\n453\t        \"Typecheck passes\"\n454\t      ],\n455\t      \"priority\": 20,\n456\t      \"passes\": true,\n457\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n458\t      \"tags\": [\n459\t        \"ui\"\n460\t      ]\n461\t    },\n462\t    {\n463\t      \"id\": \"US-021\",\n464\t      \"title\": \"Keyboard shortcuts + shortcuts modal\",\n465\t      \"description\": \"As a learner, I want comprehensive keyboard navigation in the lesson view and a shortcuts modal showing all bindings, so I can move through lessons without a mouse.\",\n466\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n467\t        \"Global hook src/lib/hooks/useKeyboardShortcuts.ts registers handlers; ignores keys when active element is input/textarea/contentEditable/CodeMirror\",\n468\t        \"Lesson view shortcuts: j or ↓ → next section (smooth scroll to next #section-…), k or ↑ → previous section, ⌘B → toggle TOC, ⌘. → toggle tutor (no-op visible state in MVP), Space → mark current section complete (if section supports it), n → next lesson when current marked complete, p → previous lesson, f → focus mode (collapses both panels)\",\n469\t        \"Global: '?' opens shortcuts modal, Esc closes any open modal\",\n470\t        \"Shortcuts modal: list grouped by category (Global / Lesson / Code editor / Chat composer); each row shows the key combo (in --font-mono in a small pill) + action description; styled per design tokens with --bg-elevated, --radius-xl, max-width 520px, 1px --border; backdrop blur-sm + 50% black overlay; click backdrop or Esc closes\",\n471\t        \"@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) disables smooth scrolling triggered by j/k\",\n472\t        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: press '?', screenshot modal in light + dark; press Esc, confirm closed; press 'j' in a lesson, confirm scrollY increases\",\n473\t        \"Typecheck passes\"\n474\t      ],\n475\t      \"priority\": 21,\n476\t      \"passes\": true,\n477\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n478\t      \"tags\": [\n479\t        \"ui\"\n480\t      ]\n481\t    },\n482\t    {\n483\t      \"id\": \"US-022\",\n484\t      \"title\": \"Inline edit for Theory widget — markdown editor + preview\",\n485\t      \"description\": \"As a course author, I want to edit theory markdown directly in the lesson view with a live preview so I can polish content without leaving the app.\",\n486\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n487\t        \"Theory widget header gets an 'Edit' icon button (pencil) in addition to existing controls\",\n488\t        \"Click 'Edit' → swaps body to a CodeMirror block with markdown syntax highlighting, seeded with current `markdown` field\",\n489\t        \"Toggle within edit mode: 'Write' / 'Preview' segmented control; Preview renders the same react-markdown + KaTeX pipeline used in read mode\",\n490\t        \"Footer in edit mode: 'Cancel' (ghost — reverts to original, exits edit mode) | 'Save' (primary — disabled if content unchanged)\",\n491\t        \"Save → PUT /api/courses/[slug]/lessons/[lessonSlug] with the section's markdown patched; on success, exits edit mode and re-renders with new content\",\n492\t        \"On save error (e.g. validation): show inline Callout in danger tone; do not exit edit mode\",\n493\t        \"Editing one section does not lose unsaved edits in another section (per-section local state)\",\n494\t        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: click Edit, change text, toggle Preview, save, reload page, confirm new text persists\",\n495\t        \"Typecheck passes\"\n496\t      ],\n497\t      \"priority\": 22,\n498\t      \"passes\": true,\n499\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n500\t      \"tags\": [\n501\t        \"ui\"\n502\t      ]\n503\t    },\n504\t    {\n505\t      \"id\": \"US-023\",\n506\t      \"title\": \"Edit widget params — generic forms for quiz / code / demo / sandbox\",\n507\t      \"description\": \"As a course author, I want a per-widget editor for parameters (questions, options, starter code, tests, sigma defaults, etc.) so I can tweak generated content without editing JSON by hand.\",\n508\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n509\t        \"Each non-theory widget gets an 'Edit' icon button (pencil) in its header\",\n510\t        \"Click 'Edit' → opens a side panel (320px from the right edge, slides over content) with a form rendered for the specific widget type\",\n511\t        \"Quiz editor: question textarea, options list (each row: option text + 'correct' checkbox + drag handle + remove button), 'Add option' button, multiSelect toggle, explanation textarea\",\n512\t        \"Code editor: task description (markdown textarea), starter code (CodeMirror Python), tests list — each test row: name input + body (CodeMirror Python collapsible per-row) + remove button, 'Add test' button\",\n513\t        \"Demo editor: image src dropdown (auto-populated from /public/demo-images/), sigmaMin / sigmaMax / sigmaDefault number inputs\",\n514\t        \"Sandbox editor: starter code (CodeMirror) + encouragement text input\",\n515\t        \"Footer: 'Cancel' (ghost) + 'Save' (primary, disabled when content unchanged)\",\n516\t        \"Save → PUT lesson JSON via API; success closes panel and re-renders widget with new data\",\n517\t        \"Validation: client-side Zod parse before sending PUT; field-level error messages rendered inline in red below the offending input\",\n518\t        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: edit a quiz's options (rename, mark different one correct, save), retake the quiz with the new options, confirm correct/incorrect logic still works\",\n519\t        \"Typecheck passes\"\n520\t      ],\n521\t      \"priority\": 23,\n522\t      \"passes\": true,"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9bf3d4c0-be72-4235-a7a7-0162ef2f8d69","uuid":"b8988705-3bd7-483a-9d36-6539b0bbef69","timestamp":"2026-05-04T07:08:38.548Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/nukeemann/projects/ai_lecturer/.worktrees/US-056/scripts/ralph/prd.json","content":"      \"id\": \"US-014\",\n      \"title\": \"Dashboard — course grid + Continue learning hero + New course CTA\",\n      \"description\": \"As a learner, I want a home screen showing my courses and a clear way to create new ones so I know where to start each session.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Route / is the dashboard\",\n        \"Top header (64px): logo/app name left, search input centered (decorative placeholder for MVP — no behavior), theme toggle slot + settings icon + avatar right\",\n        \"Max-width 1080px content area, padding var(--space-7) var(--space-6)\",\n        \"'Continue learning' hero card visible only when at least one course has lastVisitedAt: full content-width, --radius-xl, --bg-elevated, 1px --border; left side has accent-tinted course icon + breadcrumb + lesson title (--fs-2xl weight 600); right side has big 'Resume' primary button → routes to /courses/[slug]/lessons/[lessonSlug]\",\n        \"When no progress, hero is hidden (no stub)\",\n        \"Course grid: CSS grid `repeat(auto-fill, minmax(320px, 1fr))`, gap var(--space-5)\",\n        \"Each card: --bg-elevated, --radius-lg, 1px --border, padding var(--space-5); 36px round icon (color = course's accentColor from schema, lucide icon from course.icon); title (--fs-lg weight 600); 1-line description; status badge ('New' / 'In progress · X/Y' / 'Completed'); 4px progress bar at bottom\",\n        \"Hover: border darkens to --border-strong + subtle --shadow-sm lift\",\n        \"Empty state (when 0 courses): replace grid with centered 'Create your first course' card (--bg-elevated, --radius-xl, padding generous) + 4 starter topic chips ('Linear algebra basics', 'How transformers work', 'Computer vision basics', 'Bayesian statistics') — chips route to /create with topic prefilled via query string\",\n        \"'+ Nowy kurs' primary button top-right of content area, routes to /create\",\n        \"Dashboard re-fetches GET /api/courses + GET /api/progress on mount; refetch on window focus\",\n        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: with 0 courses → empty state visible; with mock courses + progress → grid + hero render; click a card → navigates to lesson\",\n        \"Typecheck passes\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 14,\n      \"passes\": true,\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"ui\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-015\",\n      \"title\": \"Lesson view shell — 3-col layout + toolbar + bottom bar placeholders\",\n      \"description\": \"As a learner, I want a 3-column lesson layout with a top toolbar and bottom bar so the full notebook-style learning surface is in place for content + navigation.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Route /courses/[slug]/lessons/[lessonSlug] renders the lesson shell\",\n        \"CSS grid: grid-template-columns: <tocCol> minmax(0,1fr) <chatCol>, rows '52px 1fr 56px'; tocCol = 276px expanded / 52px collapsed; chatCol = 320px when chat open / 0 when closed (chat closed by default in MVP)\",\n        \"Toolbar 52px: breadcrumb left ('Course › Module › Lesson', lesson name in --text, others --text-tertiary, --fs-sm, clickable), spacer flex-1, section progress pill (N/M mono in --bg-subtle 1px --border --radius-md padding 4px 10px) + 60×4px segmented progress bar, vertical 1px×22px --border divider, theme toggle slot, icon button '?' for shortcuts, icon button '⌘.' for tutor (disabled / greyed in MVP since tutor not implemented)\",\n        \"Right column placeholder: empty <aside> with width 0 in MVP; when expanded, shows a single centered note 'AI tutor — coming soon'\",\n        \"Bottom bar 56px: empty placeholder for prev/mark/next (filled in US-018)\",\n        \"Center column: ready to host content stream from US-017\",\n        \"Lesson data fetched from GET /api/courses/[slug]/lessons/[lessonSlug] on mount; loading state = skeleton bars (3 stacked bars matching widget heights) in content area; error state = Callout 'Lesson not found' with link back to course\",\n        \"On lesson mount: PATCH /api/progress with { courseSlug, lessonSlug, status: 'started', markVisited: true } — but only update status if currently 'not_started' (don't downgrade 'finished' to 'started')\",\n        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: navigate to a stub lesson, confirm 3-col layout + toolbar + bottom bar render in both light and dark\",\n        \"Typecheck passes\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 15,\n      \"passes\": true,\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"ui\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-016\",\n      \"title\": \"TOC sidebar — modules, lessons, status dots, collapse\",\n      \"description\": \"As a learner, I want a left sidebar listing all modules and lessons in this course with my progress status, so I can navigate at any time.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Left column 276px expanded, 52px collapsed; toggle persists to localStorage['toc-collapsed']\",\n        \"Header: 'All courses' eyebrow link (back to dashboard, --fs-xs uppercase letter-spacing 0.06em weight 600 --text-tertiary) above course title (--fs-sm weight 600)\",\n        \"Each module is a collapsible group with header (--fs-sm weight 600) and chevron; click toggles expansion of its lessons\",\n        \"Each lesson row: 28px tall, padding 0 12px, --fs-sm, gap-2 between status dot + label, label truncated with ellipsis on overflow\",\n        \"Status dot 6px circle: --success solid (finished), --accent solid (started), --border-strong hollow ring (not_started); reads from progress\",\n        \"Active lesson row: --accent-subtle bg, label color --accent-text, weight 600, 2px-wide left accent border bleeding into row\",\n        \"Click on lesson row → router.push to that lesson\",\n        \"Collapsed state (52px): only status dots visible vertically stacked; hover on dot → tooltip with lesson title\",\n        \"180ms width transition on collapse/expand\",\n        \"Toggle button (icon-only chevron) in TOC header right-side\",\n        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: render lesson with course of 2 modules × 3 lessons, click another lesson → confirm navigation; toggle collapse → confirm width animation + tooltips on dots\",\n        \"Typecheck passes\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 16,\n      \"passes\": true,\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"ui\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-017\",\n      \"title\": \"Content stream — lesson header + widgets in order\",\n      \"description\": \"As a learner, I want the lesson content to flow as a vertical stack of typed widgets so each section is self-contained and the lesson reads like a notebook.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Center column: vertical scroll, max-content-width 760px, centered, with --space-6 horizontal padding\",\n        \"Lesson header above first widget: eyebrow 'Module N · Lesson M' (--fs-xs uppercase letter-spacing 0.06em weight 600 --text-tertiary), H1 lesson title (--fs-3xl weight 600 letter-spacing -0.02em), 1-line description (--text-secondary --fs-md)\",\n        \"Section widgets stacked with var(--space-section) gaps; rendered by looking up section.type in widgetRegistry and rendering its component with section.data\",\n        \"Each section gets id='section-<sectionId>' so TOC + scrollIntoView + URL hash navigation can target it\",\n        \"Unknown widget type renders a fallback Callout 'Unsupported widget type: <type>' (warning tone)\",\n        \"Section number (§N) auto-derived from index in lesson.sections[]\",\n        \"Widget header status badge derived per section from progress.sectionState (if any) or from completion auto-detection (e.g. quiz answered correctly, code submitted passing)\",\n        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: render a lesson stub with all 5 widget types in sequence, confirm all render with correct accent rails and spacing\",\n        \"Typecheck passes\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 17,\n      \"passes\": true,\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"ui\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-018\",\n      \"title\": \"Bottom bar — prev / mark complete / next + auto-advance\",\n      \"description\": \"As a learner, I want prev/next navigation and a Mark complete button at the bottom of every lesson so I can move through the course at my own pace.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Bottom bar 56px filled per design\",\n        \"Prev button (left, ghost): eyebrow 'Previous' + previous lesson title (truncated); disabled when first lesson in course; click → router.push to prev lesson\",\n        \"Center: 'Mark lesson complete' button — primary if lesson status !== 'finished', otherwise rendered as 'Lesson completed' with check icon (ghost styling)\",\n        \"Click on Mark complete → PATCH /api/progress with { status: 'finished' }, button morphs to 'Lesson completed'\",\n        \"Next button (right, ghost): eyebrow 'Next' + next lesson title; disabled when last lesson; click → router.push to next lesson\",\n        \"Auto-advance: when 'Mark complete' clicked AND a next lesson exists in this course, after 600ms fade-out animation, router.push to next lesson\",\n        \"Prev/next resolution: walk course.modules → flatten to ordered list of lessons across all modules in display order, find current lesson index, prev = index-1 if exists, next = index+1 if exists\",\n        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: navigate to middle lesson, click Mark complete, observe 600ms fade + auto-advance to next; confirm finished status persists\",\n        \"Typecheck passes\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 18,\n      \"passes\": true,\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"ui\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-019\",\n      \"title\": \"Progress wiring — TOC dots + dashboard cards/hero stay in sync\",\n      \"description\": \"As a learner, I want my progress (started/finished) reflected consistently in the TOC dots, dashboard cards, and Continue learning hero so the UI never lies about my state.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"All three surfaces (TOC, dashboard cards, dashboard hero) read the same GET /api/progress endpoint and reflect current status\",\n        \"Course card status badge derived as: 0 lessons started → 'New'; any started but not all finished → 'In progress · X/Y' (X=finished count, Y=total lessons); all finished → 'Completed'\",\n        \"Course card progress bar fill = finishedCount / totalLessons\",\n        \"Continue learning hero on dashboard reads lastVisitedAt across all courses, picks the one with the latest timestamp, shows its lastVisitedLessonSlug\",\n        \"When the user clicks Mark complete in lesson view (US-018) and returns to dashboard via prev navigation or 'All courses' link, dashboard reflects new status without manual refresh (refetch on focus is enough)\",\n        \"TOC dots in lesson view live-update when current lesson is marked complete (no full reload required)\",\n        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: complete one lesson, return to dashboard, confirm card badge changes to 'In progress · 1/N' and hero shows that course\",\n        \"Typecheck passes\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 19,\n      \"passes\": true,\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"ui\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-020\",\n      \"title\": \"Theme toggle (light/dark) in dashboard header + lesson toolbar\",\n      \"description\": \"As a learner, I want a sun/moon button in both the dashboard header and the lesson toolbar to switch between light and dark mode, with my choice remembered.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"<ThemeToggle /> component renders a 28px icon button: shows sun icon when current data-theme='dark' (clicking → switches to light), moon icon when current data-theme='light' (clicking → switches to dark)\",\n        \"Click toggles <html data-theme> attribute and persists choice to localStorage['theme']\",\n        \"On app boot: an inline blocking script in <head> reads localStorage['theme'] and applies before React hydrates (prevents FOUC); fallback: prefers-color-scheme when localStorage['theme'] unset\",\n        \"Mounted in dashboard header (between settings and avatar) AND in lesson toolbar (between section progress pill and shortcuts button '?')\",\n        \"120ms transition on icon swap (opacity + 180° rotate)\",\n        \"Respects prefers-color-scheme on first load only; subsequent loads honor user's last manual choice\",\n        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: load dashboard in light mode, click toggle, confirm CSS vars switch (background changes, all sample swatches recolor); reload page, confirm dark mode persisted; same flow inside a lesson view\",\n        \"Typecheck passes\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 20,\n      \"passes\": true,\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"ui\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-021\",\n      \"title\": \"Keyboard shortcuts + shortcuts modal\",\n      \"description\": \"As a learner, I want comprehensive keyboard navigation in the lesson view and a shortcuts modal showing all bindings, so I can move through lessons without a mouse.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Global hook src/lib/hooks/useKeyboardShortcuts.ts registers handlers; ignores keys when active element is input/textarea/contentEditable/CodeMirror\",\n        \"Lesson view shortcuts: j or ↓ → next section (smooth scroll to next #section-…), k or ↑ → previous section, ⌘B → toggle TOC, ⌘. → toggle tutor (no-op visible state in MVP), Space → mark current section complete (if section supports it), n → next lesson when current marked complete, p → previous lesson, f → focus mode (collapses both panels)\",\n        \"Global: '?' opens shortcuts modal, Esc closes any open modal\",\n        \"Shortcuts modal: list grouped by category (Global / Lesson / Code editor / Chat composer); each row shows the key combo (in --font-mono in a small pill) + action description; styled per design tokens with --bg-elevated, --radius-xl, max-width 520px, 1px --border; backdrop blur-sm + 50% black overlay; click backdrop or Esc closes\",\n        \"@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) disables smooth scrolling triggered by j/k\",\n        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: press '?', screenshot modal in light + dark; press Esc, confirm closed; press 'j' in a lesson, confirm scrollY increases\",\n        \"Typecheck passes\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 21,\n      \"passes\": true,\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"ui\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-022\",\n      \"title\": \"Inline edit for Theory widget — markdown editor + preview\",\n      \"description\": \"As a course author, I want to edit theory markdown directly in the lesson view with a live preview so I can polish content without leaving the app.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Theory widget header gets an 'Edit' icon button (pencil) in addition to existing controls\",\n        \"Click 'Edit' → swaps body to a CodeMirror block with markdown syntax highlighting, seeded with current `markdown` field\",\n        \"Toggle within edit mode: 'Write' / 'Preview' segmented control; Preview renders the same react-markdown + KaTeX pipeline used in read mode\",\n        \"Footer in edit mode: 'Cancel' (ghost — reverts to original, exits edit mode) | 'Save' (primary — disabled if content unchanged)\",\n        \"Save → PUT /api/courses/[slug]/lessons/[lessonSlug] with the section's markdown patched; on success, exits edit mode and re-renders with new content\",\n        \"On save error (e.g. validation): show inline Callout in danger tone; do not exit edit mode\",\n        \"Editing one section does not lose unsaved edits in another section (per-section local state)\",\n        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: click Edit, change text, toggle Preview, save, reload page, confirm new text persists\",\n        \"Typecheck passes\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 22,\n      \"passes\": true,\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"ui\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-023\",\n      \"title\": \"Edit widget params — generic forms for quiz / code / demo / sandbox\",\n      \"description\": \"As a course author, I want a per-widget editor for parameters (questions, options, starter code, tests, sigma defaults, etc.) so I can tweak generated content without editing JSON by hand.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Each non-theory widget gets an 'Edit' icon button (pencil) in its header\",\n        \"Click 'Edit' → opens a side panel (320px from the right edge, slides over content) with a form rendered for the specific widget type\",\n        \"Quiz editor: question textarea, options list (each row: option text + 'correct' checkbox + drag handle + remove button), 'Add option' button, multiSelect toggle, explanation textarea\",\n        \"Code editor: task description (markdown textarea), starter code (CodeMirror Python), tests list — each test row: name input + body (CodeMirror Python collapsible per-row) + remove button, 'Add test' button\",\n        \"Demo editor: image src dropdown (auto-populated from /public/demo-images/), sigmaMin / sigmaMax / sigmaDefault number inputs\",\n        \"Sandbox editor: starter code (CodeMirror) + encouragement text input\",\n        \"Footer: 'Cancel' (ghost) + 'Save' (primary, disabled when content unchanged)\",\n        \"Save → PUT lesson JSON via API; success closes panel and re-renders widget with new data\",\n        \"Validation: client-side Zod parse before sending PUT; field-level error messages rendered inline in red below the offending input\",\n        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: edit a quiz's options (rename, mark different one correct, save), retake the quiz with the new options, confirm correct/incorrect logic still works\",\n        \"Typecheck passes\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 23,\n      \"passes\": true,","numLines":220,"startLine":303,"totalLines":1307}}}
