{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TB3uDYmXHwWfXjyfMGZ8cJ","type":"tool_result","content":"913\t      \"id\": \"US-042\",\n914\t      \"title\": \"Lesson count variability — extend durationTarget enum + wizard chip update\",\n915\t      \"description\": \"As a course author, I want the duration target to support short (3–5 lessons) up to comprehensive (40+ lessons) courses so the system can plan appropriately for both narrow and broad topics.\",\n916\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n917\t        \"CourseSpecSchema.durationTarget enum extended to: `'short' | 'standard' | 'extensive' | 'comprehensive'` (replaces existing `'30min' | '1h' | 'weekend'`)\",\n918\t        \"Mapping documented in src/lib/schemas/courseSpec.ts (jsdoc on field): short = 3–5 lessons / 30–60 min; standard = 8–12 lessons / 1–3h; extensive = 20–30 lessons / 5–10h; comprehensive = 40+ lessons / 15h+\",\n919\t        \"Backwards-compat parser: incoming legacy values map to new enum: '30min'→'short', '1h'→'standard', 'weekend'→'extensive' (so any pre-existing course-spec.json files still validate)\",\n920\t        \"Course creation wizard Stage 2 (US-024) duration chip selector updated from 3 to 4 chips: 'Short (3–5 lessons)' / 'Standard (8–12)' / 'Extensive (20–30)' / 'Comprehensive (40+)'\",\n921\t        \"init_course skill (scripts/ralph/skills/init_course/SKILL.md) updated: architect step uses durationTarget to bound module/lesson count when refining draftStructure; comprehensive courses generate 5–8 modules with 6–10 lessons each\",\n922\t        \"JSON Schemas regenerated via npm run build:schemas\",\n923\t        \"Vitest tests cover: parse succeeds for each new enum value; legacy values map correctly; out-of-enum value rejected\",\n924\t        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: walk through wizard Stage 2, confirm 4 chips appear, select 'Comprehensive', advance to Stage 3, confirm Stage 3 seeds 5+ modules\",\n925\t        \"Typecheck passes\",\n926\t        \"Tests pass\"\n927\t      ],\n928\t      \"priority\": 42,\n929\t      \"passes\": true,\n930\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n931\t      \"tags\": [\n932\t        \"ui\"\n933\t      ]\n934\t    },\n935\t    {\n936\t      \"id\": \"US-043\",\n937\t      \"title\": \"New widget — PlotImage (static matplotlib output + asset API route)\",\n938\t      \"description\": \"As a course author, I want a widget that displays a static PNG plot pre-rendered by matplotlib at lesson generation time, so lessons can show high-quality visualizations without requiring browser-side Python execution.\",\n939\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n940\t        \"Zod schema in src/widgets/PlotImage/schema.ts defines PlotImageData: { src: string, alt: string (required), caption?: string, sourceCode?: string, sourceLanguage?: 'python' | 'r' }\",\n941\t        \"JSON Schema regenerates via `npm run build:schemas` and is committed to src/widgets/schemas/plot-image.json\",\n942\t        \"Registry entry added in src/widgets/registry.ts; WidgetType union extended with 'plotImage'\",\n943\t        \"PlotImageSectionSchema variant added to SectionSchema discriminated union in src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts\",\n944\t        \"`--widget-plot-image` CSS var defined in both `:root[data-theme='light']` and `:root[data-theme='dark']` blocks of src/styles/tokens.css (tasteful muted color, distinct from existing widget accents)\",\n945\t        \"PlotImageEditor.tsx follows US-023 pattern (src input as text or file upload, alt input, caption input, sourceCode CodeMirror with language toggle); wired into WidgetEditPanel and SectionRenderer in lesson page\",\n946\t        \"Sample data file src/widgets/PlotImage/sample.ts exports a minimal valid instance\",\n947\t        \"Asset API route GET /api/courses/[slug]/assets/[...path] serves files from courses/<slug>/assets/; rejects path traversal via assertSafeSlug pattern; returns proper Content-Type for png/jpg/svg\",\n948\t        \"Widget renders <figure> with <img src alt /> + optional <figcaption> for caption; image max-width 100%, object-fit contain, --radius-md, 1px --border\",\n949\t        \"Collapsible 'Show source' section uses read-only CodeMirror with same theme as Code widget; sourceLanguage drives syntax highlighting; defaults to python when omitted\",\n950\t        \"PUT API endpoint accepts file upload to courses/<slug>/assets/plots/<filename>; editor wires upload via this endpoint\",\n951\t        \"Vitest unit tests cover: schema parses minimal valid object, rejects missing src/alt; asset API rejects ../ traversal\",\n952\t        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: render lesson with PlotImage section, confirm image displays in light + dark, click 'Show source' to reveal code, screenshot\",\n953\t        \"Typecheck passes\",\n954\t        \"Tests pass\"\n955\t      ],\n956\t      \"priority\": 43,\n957\t      \"passes\": true,\n958\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n959\t      \"tags\": [\n960\t        \"ui\"\n961\t      ]\n962\t    },\n963\t    {\n964\t      \"id\": \"US-044\",\n965\t      \"title\": \"New widget — PythonPlot (live matplotlib in Pyodide)\",\n966\t      \"description\": \"As a learner working with Python in lessons, I want to write code that produces a matplotlib figure and see it rendered live in the output panel, so I can experiment with visualization parameters interactively.\",\n967\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n968\t        \"Zod schema in src/widgets/PythonPlot/schema.ts defines PythonPlotData: { taskMarkdown?: string, starterCode: string, expectedFigures?: number (default 1), height?: number (canvas px) }\",\n969\t        \"JSON Schema regenerates via `npm run build:schemas`; committed to src/widgets/schemas/python-plot.json\",\n970\t        \"Registry entry added in src/widgets/registry.ts; WidgetType union extended with 'pythonPlot'\",\n971\t        \"PythonPlotSectionSchema variant added to SectionSchema discriminated union in src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts\",\n972\t        \"`--widget-python-plot` CSS var defined in both light + dark blocks of src/styles/tokens.css\",\n973\t        \"PythonPlotEditor.tsx follows US-023 pattern; wired into WidgetEditPanel and SectionRenderer\",\n974\t        \"Sample data file src/widgets/PythonPlot/sample.ts exports a minimal valid instance (e.g. plot of sin(x))\",\n975\t        \"Worker message type 'runWithPlot' accepts { code }, returns { pngBase64, stdout, error?, figureCount }\",\n976\t        \"First load: matplotlib installs lazily via pyodide.loadPackage('matplotlib'); subsequent loads skip install (singleton flag matplotlibInstalled, analogous to existing gaussInstalled pattern)\",\n977\t        \"Code injection wraps user code with: `matplotlib.use('AGG'); <user code>; plt.gcf().savefig(buf, format='png', dpi=110, bbox_inches='tight'); plt.close('all')`\",\n978\t        \"Output panel renders <img src='data:image/png;base64,...'> sized to optional height (default 360px); loading state visible while running\",\n979\t        \"Error path: Python error renders in red panel as in Code widget; figureCount=0 renders 'No figure produced — did you call plt.show() or create a figure?' hint\",\n980\t        \"Shares Pyodide namespace with other Python widgets in the same lesson (depends on US-031)\",\n981\t        \"Vitest unit tests cover: schema parses minimal valid object, rejects missing starterCode\",\n982\t        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: render PythonPlot section with sin(x) starter code, click Run, wait for matplotlib to install on first load, confirm PNG appears; modify code to plot cos(x), Run again, confirm new image\",\n983\t        \"Typecheck passes\",\n984\t        \"Tests pass\"\n985\t      ],\n986\t      \"priority\": 44,\n987\t      \"passes\": true,\n988\t      \"notes\": \"depends on US-031\",\n989\t      \"tags\": [\n990\t        \"ui\"\n991\t      ]\n992\t    },\n993\t    {\n994\t      \"id\": \"US-045\",\n995\t      \"title\": \"New widget — ParametricExplorer (generalizes Demo)\",\n996\t      \"description\": \"As a course author, I want a generalized version of the Demo widget — sliders/select/toggle params injected as Python globals into a render code block — so I can build interactive explorations beyond just Gaussian filtering.\",\n997\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n998\t        \"Zod schema in src/widgets/ParametricExplorer/schema.ts defines ParametricExplorerData: { setupCode: string, renderCode: string, params: Array<{ name, label, type: 'slider'|'select'|'toggle', min?, max?, step?, default, options? }>, outputType: 'plot'|'value'|'both', debounceMs?: number (default 150) }\",\n999\t        \"JSON Schema regenerates via `npm run build:schemas`; committed to src/widgets/schemas/parametric-explorer.json\",\n1000\t        \"Registry entry added in src/widgets/registry.ts; WidgetType union extended with 'parametricExplorer'\",\n1001\t        \"ParametricExplorerSectionSchema variant added to SectionSchema discriminated union in src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts\",\n1002\t        \"`--widget-parametric-explorer` CSS var defined in both light + dark blocks of src/styles/tokens.css\",\n1003\t        \"ParametricExplorerEditor.tsx follows US-023 pattern (param list editor with type-specific inputs, setupCode + renderCode CodeMirror Python); wired into WidgetEditPanel and SectionRenderer\",\n1004\t        \"Sample data file src/widgets/ParametricExplorer/sample.ts exports a minimal valid instance\",\n1005\t        \"Worker exposes message type 'runWithPlotParam' accepting { setupCode, renderCode, params: {[name]: value} }\",\n1006\t        \"setupCode runs once per lesson session (cached via setupCode hash in worker); renderCode runs on every param change\",\n1007\t        \"Slider input uses native setter override pattern (per progress.txt patterns) — verified by playwright that drag events fire correctly\",\n1008\t        \"Debounce 150ms by default; configurable per widget via debounceMs\",\n1009\t        \"outputType='plot' renders PNG output as in PythonPlot; outputType='value' renders text/number output from a `result` global; outputType='both' shows both stacked\",\n1010\t        \"Existing Demo widget remains unchanged — gauss-basics seed course is NOT migrated (Demo continues to work)\",\n1011\t        \"Vitest unit tests cover: schema parses minimal valid object; param injection serialization (slider→float, toggle→bool, select→string)\",\n1012\t        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: render a ParametricExplorer with one slider param affecting a sin-frequency plot, drag slider, confirm plot redraws within debounce; switch to value-output variant, confirm number updates\",\n1013\t        \"Typecheck passes\",\n1014\t        \"Tests pass\"\n1015\t      ],\n1016\t      \"priority\": 45,\n1017\t      \"passes\": true,\n1018\t      \"notes\": \"depends on US-031, US-044\",\n1019\t      \"tags\": [\n1020\t        \"ui\"\n1021\t      ]\n1022\t    },\n1023\t    {\n1024\t      \"id\": \"US-046\",\n1025\t      \"title\": \"New widget — CodeCloze (fill-in-the-blanks)\",\n1026\t      \"description\": \"As a learner with low Python syntax confidence, I want fill-in-the-blank coding exercises with per-slot validation and progressive hints, so I can focus on logic rather than fighting syntax.\",\n1027\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n1028\t        \"Zod schema in src/widgets/CodeCloze/schema.ts defines CodeClozeData: { taskMarkdown?: string, template: string (with {{slotId}} placeholders), slots: Array<{ id, hint?, validation: { kind: 'exact'|'regex'|'oneOf', value?/pattern?/values? } }>, finalTests?: Array<{ name, body, hidden? }>, hints?: Array<{ revealAfterAttempts: number, markdown: string }> }\",\n1029\t        \"JSON Schema regenerates via `npm run build:schemas`; committed to src/widgets/schemas/code-cloze.json\",\n1030\t        \"Registry entry added in src/widgets/registry.ts; WidgetType union extended with 'codeCloze'\",\n1031\t        \"CodeClozeSectionSchema variant added to SectionSchema discriminated union in src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts\",\n1032\t        \"`--widget-code-cloze` CSS var defined in both light + dark blocks of src/styles/tokens.css\",\n1033\t        \"CodeClozeEditor.tsx follows US-023 pattern (template CodeMirror Python, slots list editor with validation type per slot, finalTests editor reusing Code widget's tests editor pattern, hints list); wired into WidgetEditPanel and SectionRenderer\",\n1034\t        \"Sample data file src/widgets/CodeCloze/sample.ts exports a minimal valid instance\",\n1035\t        \"Each {{slotId}} in template renders as inline editable input sized to its current content (min 60px); other code is read-only and syntax-highlighted\",\n1036\t        \"Per-slot validation runs on blur: correct → green border + check icon, incorrect → red border + slot.hint shown inline below the slot\",\n1037\t        \"All slots correct → finalTests run in copy of lesson namespace (test isolation per US-031); pass → section marked done via PATCH /api/progress\",\n1038\t        \"Hints reveal progressively: on each failed validation attempt for a slot, count attempts; reveal the next hint from `hints` array when its revealAfterAttempts threshold is hit\",\n1039\t        \"Vitest unit tests cover: schema parses minimal valid object; per-validation kind (exact/regex/oneOf) verification\",\n1040\t        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: render a CodeCloze with 2 slots, fill one wrong, see red + hint; fix it, see green; fill the other, finalTests run; pass → status badge updates\",\n1041\t        \"Typecheck passes\",\n1042\t        \"Tests pass\"\n1043\t      ],\n1044\t      \"priority\": 46,\n1045\t      \"passes\": true,\n1046\t      \"notes\": \"depends on US-031\",\n1047\t      \"tags\": [\n1048\t        \"ui\"\n1049\t      ]\n1050\t    },\n1051\t    {\n1052\t      \"id\": \"US-047\",\n1053\t      \"title\": \"New widget — DragMatch (drag items to zones)\",\n1054\t      \"description\": \"As a course author, I want a drag-and-drop matching widget for term↔definition, category↔example, label↔diagram, so I can author varied recall exercises with low friction.\",\n1055\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n1056\t        \"Zod schema in src/widgets/DragMatch/schema.ts defines DragMatchData: { prompt: string, items: Array<{id, label}>, zones: Array<{id, label, accepts: string[]}>, multipleItemsPerZone?: boolean (default false), explanation?: string }\",\n1057\t        \"JSON Schema regenerates via `npm run build:schemas`; committed to src/widgets/schemas/drag-match.json\",\n1058\t        \"Registry entry added in src/widgets/registry.ts; WidgetType union extended with 'dragMatch'\",\n1059\t        \"DragMatchSectionSchema variant added to SectionSchema discriminated union in src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts\",\n1060\t        \"`--widget-drag-match` CSS var defined in both light + dark blocks of src/styles/tokens.css\",\n1061\t        \"DragMatchEditor.tsx follows US-023 pattern (items list editor, zones list editor with multi-select for accepts, multipleItemsPerZone toggle, explanation textarea); wired into WidgetEditPanel and SectionRenderer\",\n1062\t        \"Sample data file src/widgets/DragMatch/sample.ts exports a minimal valid instance\",\n1063\t        \"Dependency added to package.json: @dnd-kit/core + @dnd-kit/sortable (run `npm install` and commit lockfile)\",\n1064\t        \"Items draggable from item bank panel (top); zones are valid drop targets with visual hover highlight (--accent-subtle bg) when an item is being dragged over\",\n1065\t        \"Submit button validates: each zone contains exactly the items in `accepts` (multipleItemsPerZone respected for ordering)\",\n1066\t        \"Visual feedback after submit: correct zones --success-border + --success-subtle; wrong zones --danger-border + --danger-subtle; misplaced item gets a subtle outline pointing back to its expected zone\",\n1067\t        \"Explanation always shown after submit (Callout-styled, neutral tone — per Quiz widget pattern)\",\n1068\t        \"Keyboard accessibility: dnd-kit's keyboard sensors enabled (Tab+Space to lift, arrows to move, Space to drop)\",\n1069\t        \"Section status auto-becomes 'done' on first all-correct submission (PATCH /api/progress)\",\n1070\t        \"Vitest unit tests cover: schema parses minimal valid object; correctness validation logic (single-zone and multi-zone)\",\n1071\t        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: render DragMatch with 3 items + 3 zones, drag one wrong, submit, see red feedback + explanation; rearrange, submit, see green + status badge updates\",\n1072\t        \"Typecheck passes\",\n1073\t        \"Tests pass\"\n1074\t      ],\n1075\t      \"priority\": 47,\n1076\t      \"passes\": true,\n1077\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n1078\t      \"tags\": [\n1079\t        \"ui\"\n1080\t      ]\n1081\t    },\n1082\t    {\n1083\t      \"id\": \"US-048\",\n1084\t      \"title\": \"New widget — DataTable (sortable, filterable, paginated)\",\n1085\t      \"description\": \"As a course author, I want a sortable/filterable table widget so I can present datasets, results, or comparisons inline in lessons.\",\n1086\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n1087\t        \"Zod schema in src/widgets/DataTable/schema.ts defines DataTableData: { columns: Array<{ key, label, type?: 'string'|'number'|'boolean', sortable? (default true), filterable? (default false) }>, rows: Array<Record<string, string|number|boolean|null>>, initialSort?: { key, dir: 'asc'|'desc' }, pageSize?: number (default 25) }\",\n1088\t        \"JSON Schema regenerates via `npm run build:schemas`; committed to src/widgets/schemas/data-table.json\",\n1089\t        \"Registry entry added in src/widgets/registry.ts; WidgetType union extended with 'dataTable'\",\n1090\t        \"DataTableSectionSchema variant added to SectionSchema discriminated union in src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts\",\n1091\t        \"`--widget-data-table` CSS var defined in both light + dark blocks of src/styles/tokens.css\",\n1092\t        \"DataTableEditor.tsx follows US-023 pattern (columns list editor with type/sortable/filterable per column, rows editor as JSON textarea with live validation, pageSize input); wired into WidgetEditPanel and SectionRenderer\",\n1093\t        \"Sample data file src/widgets/DataTable/sample.ts exports a minimal valid instance\",\n1094\t        \"Click column header → sort ascending; second click → descending; third click → unsorted (back to row insertion order); sort indicator chevron shown next to header label\",\n1095\t        \"Filter input per filterable column (text contains for string type, range min/max inputs for number type)\",\n1096\t        \"Pagination controls if rows.length > pageSize: prev/next buttons + 'Page X of Y' indicator centered below table\",\n1097\t        \"Numeric columns formatted via toLocaleString() for thousand separators; boolean columns render as ✓/—\",\n1098\t        \"Sticky header on scroll within table body (when table height exceeds viewport portion)\",\n1099\t        \"Vitest unit tests cover: schema parses minimal valid object; sort logic (asc/desc/unsorted); filter logic (string contains + number range)\",\n1100\t        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: render DataTable with 30 rows × 4 cols, click sort on numeric column, confirm rows reorder; filter a string column, confirm rows hidden; navigate pagination\",\n1101\t        \"Typecheck passes\",\n1102\t        \"Tests pass\"\n1103\t      ],\n1104\t      \"priority\": 48,\n1105\t      \"passes\": true,\n1106\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n1107\t      \"tags\": [\n1108\t        \"ui\"\n1109\t      ]\n1110\t    },\n1111\t    {\n1112\t      \"id\": \"US-049\",\n1113\t      \"title\": \"New widget — Video (YouTube/MP4 with clickable transcript)\",\n1114\t      \"description\": \"As a course author, I want to embed YouTube or MP4 videos with optional clickable transcripts, so external high-quality content (3Blue1Brown, StatQuest) can supplement lessons.\",\n1115\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n1116\t        \"Zod schema in src/widgets/Video/schema.ts defines VideoData: { kind: 'youtube'|'mp4', src: string, title?, durationSeconds?, transcript?: Array<{tStart: number, tEnd?: number, text: string, speaker?: string}>, autoplay? (default false), startAt?: number }\",\n1117\t        \"JSON Schema regenerates via `npm run build:schemas`; committed to src/widgets/schemas/video.json\",\n1118\t        \"Registry entry added in src/widgets/registry.ts; WidgetType union extended with 'video'\",\n1119\t        \"VideoSectionSchema variant added to SectionSchema discriminated union in src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts\",\n1120\t        \"`--widget-video` CSS var defined in both light + dark blocks of src/styles/tokens.css\",\n1121\t        \"VideoEditor.tsx follows US-023 pattern (kind toggle, src input, optional title/duration/startAt/autoplay, transcript list editor with tStart/tEnd/text/speaker per row); wired into WidgetEditPanel and SectionRenderer\",\n1122\t        \"Sample data file src/widgets/Video/sample.ts exports a minimal valid instance\",\n1123\t        \"YouTube: embed via <iframe src='https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/<id>?...'> with proper width/height responsive container (16:9 aspect-ratio CSS); src may be a video ID or a YouTube URL (parser extracts ID)\",\n1124\t        \"MP4: HTML5 <video controls> tag; supports MP4 hosted in courses/<slug>/assets/ via the asset API route from US-043\",\n1125\t        \"startAt parameter passes ?start=<sec> for YouTube and currentTime=<sec> for video element on load\",\n1126\t        \"Transcript panel (collapsible) renders below video; click on segment seeks player to tStart (postMessage to YouTube iframe API; currentTime= for MP4)\",\n1127\t        \"Active transcript segment highlights as player progresses (--accent-subtle bg) — driven by timeupdate listener (MP4) or YouTube iframe API\",\n1128\t        \"Speaker labels rendered as small uppercase prefix when present (--text-tertiary --fs-xs weight 600 letter-spacing 0.06em)\",\n1129\t        \"Vitest unit tests cover: schema parses minimal valid object (both kinds); YouTube ID extraction from URL formats\",\n1130\t        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: render YouTube embed with transcript, click a transcript segment, confirm player seeks (test via window.postMessage spy or iframe currentTime check)\",\n1131\t        \"Typecheck passes\",\n1132\t        \"Tests pass\"\n1133\t      ],\n1134\t      \"priority\": 49,\n1135\t      \"passes\": true,\n1136\t      \"notes\": \"\",\n1137\t      \"tags\": [\n1138\t        \"ui\"\n1139\t      ]\n1140\t    },\n1141\t    {\n1142\t      \"id\": \"US-050\",\n1143\t      \"title\": \"New widget — Image (URL src + local prefetch cache)\",\n1144\t      \"description\": \"As a course author, I want an Image widget that takes a URL and locally caches the image into the course's assets folder on first save, so lessons remain available offline and source attribution is preserved.\",\n1145\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n1146\t        \"Zod schema in src/widgets/Image/schema.ts defines ImageData: { src: string (URL or local relative path), alt: string (required), caption?: string, attribution?: { text: string, url?: string }, maxWidth?: string (px or %, default '100%') }\",\n1147\t        \"JSON Schema regenerates via `npm run build:schemas`; committed to src/widgets/schemas/image.json\",\n1148\t        \"Registry entry added in src/widgets/registry.ts; WidgetType union extended with 'image'\",\n1149\t        \"ImageSectionSchema variant added to SectionSchema discriminated union in src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts\",\n1150\t        \"`--widget-image` CSS var defined in both light + dark blocks of src/styles/tokens.css\",\n1151\t        \"ImageEditor.tsx follows US-023 pattern (src input as text URL, alt input, caption textarea, attribution.text + attribution.url, maxWidth input); wired into WidgetEditPanel and SectionRenderer\",\n1152\t        \"Sample data file src/widgets/Image/sample.ts exports a minimal valid instance\",\n1153\t        \"On lesson save (PUT /api/courses/[slug]/lessons/[lessonSlug]): if any Image section has an external URL src (http/https), server-side fetch the image, store in courses/<slug>/assets/images/<sha256(url).slice(0,16)>.<ext>, rewrite src in saved JSON to local relative path '/api/courses/<slug>/assets/images/<filename>'\",\n1154\t        \"Asset API route extends US-043 to serve courses/<slug>/assets/images/ subdirectory\",\n1155\t        \"Widget renders <figure>: <img src alt style={{maxWidth}}> + optional <figcaption> with caption text + attribution (linked if attribution.url present, plain text otherwise)\",\n1156\t        \"Caching is idempotent: same URL hashes to same filename → no duplicate downloads\",\n1157\t        \"Failed fetch on save: log warning, keep original URL in saved JSON (graceful degradation), return 200 with a warning field in response body\",\n1158\t        \"Vitest tests cover: schema parses minimal valid object; hash-based filename generation; URL→local rewrite happy path; failed-fetch graceful path\",\n1159\t        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: render lesson with Image section using a local cached path, confirm image displays in light + dark with caption + attribution link\",\n1160\t        \"Typecheck passes\",\n1161\t        \"Tests pass\"\n1162\t      ],\n1163\t      \"priority\": 50,\n1164\t      \"passes\": true,\n1165\t      \"notes\": \"Caches at lesson-save time, not at view time. Path traversal protected via assertSafeSlug.\",\n1166\t      \"tags\": [\n1167\t        \"ui\"\n1168\t      ]\n1169\t    },\n1170\t    {\n1171\t      \"id\": \"US-051\",\n1172\t      \"title\": \"Update generate_lesson skill — encourage inline markdown images + Image widget for key illustrations\",\n1173\t      \"description\": \"As an agent generating lessons, I want explicit guidance to use inline markdown images and the Image widget for key illustrations, so generated lessons are visually rich rather than wall-of-text.\",\n1174\t      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n1175\t        \"scripts/ralph/skills/generate_lesson/SKILL.md updated with a new section 'Visual Illustrations' immediately after the Source Research section from US-041\",\n1176\t        \"Skill instructs: every theory section ≥300 chars long should include at least one inline markdown image `![alt](url)` where it makes pedagogical sense\",\n1177\t        \"Skill instructs: use the Image widget (US-050) as a standalone section for hero illustrations, diagrams, or figures that warrant their own caption + attribution treatment\",\n1178\t        \"Skill instructs: prefer Wikimedia Commons, public-domain repositories, official documentation diagrams (scikit-image, OpenCV, matplotlib), arxiv figure references; AVOID hotlinking from blog hosts likely to break (medium, towardsdatascience, personal blogs)\",\n1179\t        \"Skill instructs: every image (inline or widget) MUST have meaningful alt text describing what is shown — never empty alt, never 'image' placeholder\",\n1180\t        \"Skill instructs: provide attribution for Image widget when source mandates (Wikimedia → 'Wikimedia Commons, <author>, <license>')\",\n1181\t        \"Worked example in SKILL.md updated to include one inline markdown image (with Wikimedia URL) and one Image widget section\",\n1182\t        \"Typecheck passes\"\n1183\t      ],\n1184\t      \"priority\": 51,\n1185\t      \"passes\": true,\n1186\t      \"notes\": \"Skill-only changes (markdown + worked examples).\",\n1187\t      \"tags\": []\n1188\t    },\n1189\t    {\n1190\t      \"id\": \"US-052\",\n1191\t      \"title\": \"LessonChat — sliding side panel UI scaffold + persisted draft in localStorage\",\n1192\t      \"description\": \"As a learner, I want a sliding side panel inside lessons where I can compose questions to an AI tutor and have my draft preserved across page reloads, so I can come back to a question without retyping.\","}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9bf3d4c0-be72-4235-a7a7-0162ef2f8d69","uuid":"e36f33d9-f4ce-4964-9c34-a6a0c775f602","timestamp":"2026-05-04T07:08:43.258Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/nukeemann/projects/ai_lecturer/.worktrees/US-056/scripts/ralph/prd.json","content":"      \"id\": \"US-042\",\n      \"title\": \"Lesson count variability — extend durationTarget enum + wizard chip update\",\n      \"description\": \"As a course author, I want the duration target to support short (3–5 lessons) up to comprehensive (40+ lessons) courses so the system can plan appropriately for both narrow and broad topics.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"CourseSpecSchema.durationTarget enum extended to: `'short' | 'standard' | 'extensive' | 'comprehensive'` (replaces existing `'30min' | '1h' | 'weekend'`)\",\n        \"Mapping documented in src/lib/schemas/courseSpec.ts (jsdoc on field): short = 3–5 lessons / 30–60 min; standard = 8–12 lessons / 1–3h; extensive = 20–30 lessons / 5–10h; comprehensive = 40+ lessons / 15h+\",\n        \"Backwards-compat parser: incoming legacy values map to new enum: '30min'→'short', '1h'→'standard', 'weekend'→'extensive' (so any pre-existing course-spec.json files still validate)\",\n        \"Course creation wizard Stage 2 (US-024) duration chip selector updated from 3 to 4 chips: 'Short (3–5 lessons)' / 'Standard (8–12)' / 'Extensive (20–30)' / 'Comprehensive (40+)'\",\n        \"init_course skill (scripts/ralph/skills/init_course/SKILL.md) updated: architect step uses durationTarget to bound module/lesson count when refining draftStructure; comprehensive courses generate 5–8 modules with 6–10 lessons each\",\n        \"JSON Schemas regenerated via npm run build:schemas\",\n        \"Vitest tests cover: parse succeeds for each new enum value; legacy values map correctly; out-of-enum value rejected\",\n        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: walk through wizard Stage 2, confirm 4 chips appear, select 'Comprehensive', advance to Stage 3, confirm Stage 3 seeds 5+ modules\",\n        \"Typecheck passes\",\n        \"Tests pass\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 42,\n      \"passes\": true,\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"ui\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-043\",\n      \"title\": \"New widget — PlotImage (static matplotlib output + asset API route)\",\n      \"description\": \"As a course author, I want a widget that displays a static PNG plot pre-rendered by matplotlib at lesson generation time, so lessons can show high-quality visualizations without requiring browser-side Python execution.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Zod schema in src/widgets/PlotImage/schema.ts defines PlotImageData: { src: string, alt: string (required), caption?: string, sourceCode?: string, sourceLanguage?: 'python' | 'r' }\",\n        \"JSON Schema regenerates via `npm run build:schemas` and is committed to src/widgets/schemas/plot-image.json\",\n        \"Registry entry added in src/widgets/registry.ts; WidgetType union extended with 'plotImage'\",\n        \"PlotImageSectionSchema variant added to SectionSchema discriminated union in src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts\",\n        \"`--widget-plot-image` CSS var defined in both `:root[data-theme='light']` and `:root[data-theme='dark']` blocks of src/styles/tokens.css (tasteful muted color, distinct from existing widget accents)\",\n        \"PlotImageEditor.tsx follows US-023 pattern (src input as text or file upload, alt input, caption input, sourceCode CodeMirror with language toggle); wired into WidgetEditPanel and SectionRenderer in lesson page\",\n        \"Sample data file src/widgets/PlotImage/sample.ts exports a minimal valid instance\",\n        \"Asset API route GET /api/courses/[slug]/assets/[...path] serves files from courses/<slug>/assets/; rejects path traversal via assertSafeSlug pattern; returns proper Content-Type for png/jpg/svg\",\n        \"Widget renders <figure> with <img src alt /> + optional <figcaption> for caption; image max-width 100%, object-fit contain, --radius-md, 1px --border\",\n        \"Collapsible 'Show source' section uses read-only CodeMirror with same theme as Code widget; sourceLanguage drives syntax highlighting; defaults to python when omitted\",\n        \"PUT API endpoint accepts file upload to courses/<slug>/assets/plots/<filename>; editor wires upload via this endpoint\",\n        \"Vitest unit tests cover: schema parses minimal valid object, rejects missing src/alt; asset API rejects ../ traversal\",\n        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: render lesson with PlotImage section, confirm image displays in light + dark, click 'Show source' to reveal code, screenshot\",\n        \"Typecheck passes\",\n        \"Tests pass\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 43,\n      \"passes\": true,\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"ui\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-044\",\n      \"title\": \"New widget — PythonPlot (live matplotlib in Pyodide)\",\n      \"description\": \"As a learner working with Python in lessons, I want to write code that produces a matplotlib figure and see it rendered live in the output panel, so I can experiment with visualization parameters interactively.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Zod schema in src/widgets/PythonPlot/schema.ts defines PythonPlotData: { taskMarkdown?: string, starterCode: string, expectedFigures?: number (default 1), height?: number (canvas px) }\",\n        \"JSON Schema regenerates via `npm run build:schemas`; committed to src/widgets/schemas/python-plot.json\",\n        \"Registry entry added in src/widgets/registry.ts; WidgetType union extended with 'pythonPlot'\",\n        \"PythonPlotSectionSchema variant added to SectionSchema discriminated union in src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts\",\n        \"`--widget-python-plot` CSS var defined in both light + dark blocks of src/styles/tokens.css\",\n        \"PythonPlotEditor.tsx follows US-023 pattern; wired into WidgetEditPanel and SectionRenderer\",\n        \"Sample data file src/widgets/PythonPlot/sample.ts exports a minimal valid instance (e.g. plot of sin(x))\",\n        \"Worker message type 'runWithPlot' accepts { code }, returns { pngBase64, stdout, error?, figureCount }\",\n        \"First load: matplotlib installs lazily via pyodide.loadPackage('matplotlib'); subsequent loads skip install (singleton flag matplotlibInstalled, analogous to existing gaussInstalled pattern)\",\n        \"Code injection wraps user code with: `matplotlib.use('AGG'); <user code>; plt.gcf().savefig(buf, format='png', dpi=110, bbox_inches='tight'); plt.close('all')`\",\n        \"Output panel renders <img src='data:image/png;base64,...'> sized to optional height (default 360px); loading state visible while running\",\n        \"Error path: Python error renders in red panel as in Code widget; figureCount=0 renders 'No figure produced — did you call plt.show() or create a figure?' hint\",\n        \"Shares Pyodide namespace with other Python widgets in the same lesson (depends on US-031)\",\n        \"Vitest unit tests cover: schema parses minimal valid object, rejects missing starterCode\",\n        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: render PythonPlot section with sin(x) starter code, click Run, wait for matplotlib to install on first load, confirm PNG appears; modify code to plot cos(x), Run again, confirm new image\",\n        \"Typecheck passes\",\n        \"Tests pass\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 44,\n      \"passes\": true,\n      \"notes\": \"depends on US-031\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"ui\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-045\",\n      \"title\": \"New widget — ParametricExplorer (generalizes Demo)\",\n      \"description\": \"As a course author, I want a generalized version of the Demo widget — sliders/select/toggle params injected as Python globals into a render code block — so I can build interactive explorations beyond just Gaussian filtering.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Zod schema in src/widgets/ParametricExplorer/schema.ts defines ParametricExplorerData: { setupCode: string, renderCode: string, params: Array<{ name, label, type: 'slider'|'select'|'toggle', min?, max?, step?, default, options? }>, outputType: 'plot'|'value'|'both', debounceMs?: number (default 150) }\",\n        \"JSON Schema regenerates via `npm run build:schemas`; committed to src/widgets/schemas/parametric-explorer.json\",\n        \"Registry entry added in src/widgets/registry.ts; WidgetType union extended with 'parametricExplorer'\",\n        \"ParametricExplorerSectionSchema variant added to SectionSchema discriminated union in src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts\",\n        \"`--widget-parametric-explorer` CSS var defined in both light + dark blocks of src/styles/tokens.css\",\n        \"ParametricExplorerEditor.tsx follows US-023 pattern (param list editor with type-specific inputs, setupCode + renderCode CodeMirror Python); wired into WidgetEditPanel and SectionRenderer\",\n        \"Sample data file src/widgets/ParametricExplorer/sample.ts exports a minimal valid instance\",\n        \"Worker exposes message type 'runWithPlotParam' accepting { setupCode, renderCode, params: {[name]: value} }\",\n        \"setupCode runs once per lesson session (cached via setupCode hash in worker); renderCode runs on every param change\",\n        \"Slider input uses native setter override pattern (per progress.txt patterns) — verified by playwright that drag events fire correctly\",\n        \"Debounce 150ms by default; configurable per widget via debounceMs\",\n        \"outputType='plot' renders PNG output as in PythonPlot; outputType='value' renders text/number output from a `result` global; outputType='both' shows both stacked\",\n        \"Existing Demo widget remains unchanged — gauss-basics seed course is NOT migrated (Demo continues to work)\",\n        \"Vitest unit tests cover: schema parses minimal valid object; param injection serialization (slider→float, toggle→bool, select→string)\",\n        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: render a ParametricExplorer with one slider param affecting a sin-frequency plot, drag slider, confirm plot redraws within debounce; switch to value-output variant, confirm number updates\",\n        \"Typecheck passes\",\n        \"Tests pass\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 45,\n      \"passes\": true,\n      \"notes\": \"depends on US-031, US-044\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"ui\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-046\",\n      \"title\": \"New widget — CodeCloze (fill-in-the-blanks)\",\n      \"description\": \"As a learner with low Python syntax confidence, I want fill-in-the-blank coding exercises with per-slot validation and progressive hints, so I can focus on logic rather than fighting syntax.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Zod schema in src/widgets/CodeCloze/schema.ts defines CodeClozeData: { taskMarkdown?: string, template: string (with {{slotId}} placeholders), slots: Array<{ id, hint?, validation: { kind: 'exact'|'regex'|'oneOf', value?/pattern?/values? } }>, finalTests?: Array<{ name, body, hidden? }>, hints?: Array<{ revealAfterAttempts: number, markdown: string }> }\",\n        \"JSON Schema regenerates via `npm run build:schemas`; committed to src/widgets/schemas/code-cloze.json\",\n        \"Registry entry added in src/widgets/registry.ts; WidgetType union extended with 'codeCloze'\",\n        \"CodeClozeSectionSchema variant added to SectionSchema discriminated union in src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts\",\n        \"`--widget-code-cloze` CSS var defined in both light + dark blocks of src/styles/tokens.css\",\n        \"CodeClozeEditor.tsx follows US-023 pattern (template CodeMirror Python, slots list editor with validation type per slot, finalTests editor reusing Code widget's tests editor pattern, hints list); wired into WidgetEditPanel and SectionRenderer\",\n        \"Sample data file src/widgets/CodeCloze/sample.ts exports a minimal valid instance\",\n        \"Each {{slotId}} in template renders as inline editable input sized to its current content (min 60px); other code is read-only and syntax-highlighted\",\n        \"Per-slot validation runs on blur: correct → green border + check icon, incorrect → red border + slot.hint shown inline below the slot\",\n        \"All slots correct → finalTests run in copy of lesson namespace (test isolation per US-031); pass → section marked done via PATCH /api/progress\",\n        \"Hints reveal progressively: on each failed validation attempt for a slot, count attempts; reveal the next hint from `hints` array when its revealAfterAttempts threshold is hit\",\n        \"Vitest unit tests cover: schema parses minimal valid object; per-validation kind (exact/regex/oneOf) verification\",\n        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: render a CodeCloze with 2 slots, fill one wrong, see red + hint; fix it, see green; fill the other, finalTests run; pass → status badge updates\",\n        \"Typecheck passes\",\n        \"Tests pass\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 46,\n      \"passes\": true,\n      \"notes\": \"depends on US-031\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"ui\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-047\",\n      \"title\": \"New widget — DragMatch (drag items to zones)\",\n      \"description\": \"As a course author, I want a drag-and-drop matching widget for term↔definition, category↔example, label↔diagram, so I can author varied recall exercises with low friction.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Zod schema in src/widgets/DragMatch/schema.ts defines DragMatchData: { prompt: string, items: Array<{id, label}>, zones: Array<{id, label, accepts: string[]}>, multipleItemsPerZone?: boolean (default false), explanation?: string }\",\n        \"JSON Schema regenerates via `npm run build:schemas`; committed to src/widgets/schemas/drag-match.json\",\n        \"Registry entry added in src/widgets/registry.ts; WidgetType union extended with 'dragMatch'\",\n        \"DragMatchSectionSchema variant added to SectionSchema discriminated union in src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts\",\n        \"`--widget-drag-match` CSS var defined in both light + dark blocks of src/styles/tokens.css\",\n        \"DragMatchEditor.tsx follows US-023 pattern (items list editor, zones list editor with multi-select for accepts, multipleItemsPerZone toggle, explanation textarea); wired into WidgetEditPanel and SectionRenderer\",\n        \"Sample data file src/widgets/DragMatch/sample.ts exports a minimal valid instance\",\n        \"Dependency added to package.json: @dnd-kit/core + @dnd-kit/sortable (run `npm install` and commit lockfile)\",\n        \"Items draggable from item bank panel (top); zones are valid drop targets with visual hover highlight (--accent-subtle bg) when an item is being dragged over\",\n        \"Submit button validates: each zone contains exactly the items in `accepts` (multipleItemsPerZone respected for ordering)\",\n        \"Visual feedback after submit: correct zones --success-border + --success-subtle; wrong zones --danger-border + --danger-subtle; misplaced item gets a subtle outline pointing back to its expected zone\",\n        \"Explanation always shown after submit (Callout-styled, neutral tone — per Quiz widget pattern)\",\n        \"Keyboard accessibility: dnd-kit's keyboard sensors enabled (Tab+Space to lift, arrows to move, Space to drop)\",\n        \"Section status auto-becomes 'done' on first all-correct submission (PATCH /api/progress)\",\n        \"Vitest unit tests cover: schema parses minimal valid object; correctness validation logic (single-zone and multi-zone)\",\n        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: render DragMatch with 3 items + 3 zones, drag one wrong, submit, see red feedback + explanation; rearrange, submit, see green + status badge updates\",\n        \"Typecheck passes\",\n        \"Tests pass\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 47,\n      \"passes\": true,\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"ui\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-048\",\n      \"title\": \"New widget — DataTable (sortable, filterable, paginated)\",\n      \"description\": \"As a course author, I want a sortable/filterable table widget so I can present datasets, results, or comparisons inline in lessons.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Zod schema in src/widgets/DataTable/schema.ts defines DataTableData: { columns: Array<{ key, label, type?: 'string'|'number'|'boolean', sortable? (default true), filterable? (default false) }>, rows: Array<Record<string, string|number|boolean|null>>, initialSort?: { key, dir: 'asc'|'desc' }, pageSize?: number (default 25) }\",\n        \"JSON Schema regenerates via `npm run build:schemas`; committed to src/widgets/schemas/data-table.json\",\n        \"Registry entry added in src/widgets/registry.ts; WidgetType union extended with 'dataTable'\",\n        \"DataTableSectionSchema variant added to SectionSchema discriminated union in src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts\",\n        \"`--widget-data-table` CSS var defined in both light + dark blocks of src/styles/tokens.css\",\n        \"DataTableEditor.tsx follows US-023 pattern (columns list editor with type/sortable/filterable per column, rows editor as JSON textarea with live validation, pageSize input); wired into WidgetEditPanel and SectionRenderer\",\n        \"Sample data file src/widgets/DataTable/sample.ts exports a minimal valid instance\",\n        \"Click column header → sort ascending; second click → descending; third click → unsorted (back to row insertion order); sort indicator chevron shown next to header label\",\n        \"Filter input per filterable column (text contains for string type, range min/max inputs for number type)\",\n        \"Pagination controls if rows.length > pageSize: prev/next buttons + 'Page X of Y' indicator centered below table\",\n        \"Numeric columns formatted via toLocaleString() for thousand separators; boolean columns render as ✓/—\",\n        \"Sticky header on scroll within table body (when table height exceeds viewport portion)\",\n        \"Vitest unit tests cover: schema parses minimal valid object; sort logic (asc/desc/unsorted); filter logic (string contains + number range)\",\n        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: render DataTable with 30 rows × 4 cols, click sort on numeric column, confirm rows reorder; filter a string column, confirm rows hidden; navigate pagination\",\n        \"Typecheck passes\",\n        \"Tests pass\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 48,\n      \"passes\": true,\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"ui\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-049\",\n      \"title\": \"New widget — Video (YouTube/MP4 with clickable transcript)\",\n      \"description\": \"As a course author, I want to embed YouTube or MP4 videos with optional clickable transcripts, so external high-quality content (3Blue1Brown, StatQuest) can supplement lessons.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Zod schema in src/widgets/Video/schema.ts defines VideoData: { kind: 'youtube'|'mp4', src: string, title?, durationSeconds?, transcript?: Array<{tStart: number, tEnd?: number, text: string, speaker?: string}>, autoplay? (default false), startAt?: number }\",\n        \"JSON Schema regenerates via `npm run build:schemas`; committed to src/widgets/schemas/video.json\",\n        \"Registry entry added in src/widgets/registry.ts; WidgetType union extended with 'video'\",\n        \"VideoSectionSchema variant added to SectionSchema discriminated union in src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts\",\n        \"`--widget-video` CSS var defined in both light + dark blocks of src/styles/tokens.css\",\n        \"VideoEditor.tsx follows US-023 pattern (kind toggle, src input, optional title/duration/startAt/autoplay, transcript list editor with tStart/tEnd/text/speaker per row); wired into WidgetEditPanel and SectionRenderer\",\n        \"Sample data file src/widgets/Video/sample.ts exports a minimal valid instance\",\n        \"YouTube: embed via <iframe src='https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/<id>?...'> with proper width/height responsive container (16:9 aspect-ratio CSS); src may be a video ID or a YouTube URL (parser extracts ID)\",\n        \"MP4: HTML5 <video controls> tag; supports MP4 hosted in courses/<slug>/assets/ via the asset API route from US-043\",\n        \"startAt parameter passes ?start=<sec> for YouTube and currentTime=<sec> for video element on load\",\n        \"Transcript panel (collapsible) renders below video; click on segment seeks player to tStart (postMessage to YouTube iframe API; currentTime= for MP4)\",\n        \"Active transcript segment highlights as player progresses (--accent-subtle bg) — driven by timeupdate listener (MP4) or YouTube iframe API\",\n        \"Speaker labels rendered as small uppercase prefix when present (--text-tertiary --fs-xs weight 600 letter-spacing 0.06em)\",\n        \"Vitest unit tests cover: schema parses minimal valid object (both kinds); YouTube ID extraction from URL formats\",\n        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: render YouTube embed with transcript, click a transcript segment, confirm player seeks (test via window.postMessage spy or iframe currentTime check)\",\n        \"Typecheck passes\",\n        \"Tests pass\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 49,\n      \"passes\": true,\n      \"notes\": \"\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"ui\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-050\",\n      \"title\": \"New widget — Image (URL src + local prefetch cache)\",\n      \"description\": \"As a course author, I want an Image widget that takes a URL and locally caches the image into the course's assets folder on first save, so lessons remain available offline and source attribution is preserved.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"Zod schema in src/widgets/Image/schema.ts defines ImageData: { src: string (URL or local relative path), alt: string (required), caption?: string, attribution?: { text: string, url?: string }, maxWidth?: string (px or %, default '100%') }\",\n        \"JSON Schema regenerates via `npm run build:schemas`; committed to src/widgets/schemas/image.json\",\n        \"Registry entry added in src/widgets/registry.ts; WidgetType union extended with 'image'\",\n        \"ImageSectionSchema variant added to SectionSchema discriminated union in src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts\",\n        \"`--widget-image` CSS var defined in both light + dark blocks of src/styles/tokens.css\",\n        \"ImageEditor.tsx follows US-023 pattern (src input as text URL, alt input, caption textarea, attribution.text + attribution.url, maxWidth input); wired into WidgetEditPanel and SectionRenderer\",\n        \"Sample data file src/widgets/Image/sample.ts exports a minimal valid instance\",\n        \"On lesson save (PUT /api/courses/[slug]/lessons/[lessonSlug]): if any Image section has an external URL src (http/https), server-side fetch the image, store in courses/<slug>/assets/images/<sha256(url).slice(0,16)>.<ext>, rewrite src in saved JSON to local relative path '/api/courses/<slug>/assets/images/<filename>'\",\n        \"Asset API route extends US-043 to serve courses/<slug>/assets/images/ subdirectory\",\n        \"Widget renders <figure>: <img src alt style={{maxWidth}}> + optional <figcaption> with caption text + attribution (linked if attribution.url present, plain text otherwise)\",\n        \"Caching is idempotent: same URL hashes to same filename → no duplicate downloads\",\n        \"Failed fetch on save: log warning, keep original URL in saved JSON (graceful degradation), return 200 with a warning field in response body\",\n        \"Vitest tests cover: schema parses minimal valid object; hash-based filename generation; URL→local rewrite happy path; failed-fetch graceful path\",\n        \"Verify in browser using playwright-skill: render lesson with Image section using a local cached path, confirm image displays in light + dark with caption + attribution link\",\n        \"Typecheck passes\",\n        \"Tests pass\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 50,\n      \"passes\": true,\n      \"notes\": \"Caches at lesson-save time, not at view time. Path traversal protected via assertSafeSlug.\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"ui\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-051\",\n      \"title\": \"Update generate_lesson skill — encourage inline markdown images + Image widget for key illustrations\",\n      \"description\": \"As an agent generating lessons, I want explicit guidance to use inline markdown images and the Image widget for key illustrations, so generated lessons are visually rich rather than wall-of-text.\",\n      \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\n        \"scripts/ralph/skills/generate_lesson/SKILL.md updated with a new section 'Visual Illustrations' immediately after the Source Research section from US-041\",\n        \"Skill instructs: every theory section ≥300 chars long should include at least one inline markdown image `![alt](url)` where it makes pedagogical sense\",\n        \"Skill instructs: use the Image widget (US-050) as a standalone section for hero illustrations, diagrams, or figures that warrant their own caption + attribution treatment\",\n        \"Skill instructs: prefer Wikimedia Commons, public-domain repositories, official documentation diagrams (scikit-image, OpenCV, matplotlib), arxiv figure references; AVOID hotlinking from blog hosts likely to break (medium, towardsdatascience, personal blogs)\",\n        \"Skill instructs: every image (inline or widget) MUST have meaningful alt text describing what is shown — never empty alt, never 'image' placeholder\",\n        \"Skill instructs: provide attribution for Image widget when source mandates (Wikimedia → 'Wikimedia Commons, <author>, <license>')\",\n        \"Worked example in SKILL.md updated to include one inline markdown image (with Wikimedia URL) and one Image widget section\",\n        \"Typecheck passes\"\n      ],\n      \"priority\": 51,\n      \"passes\": true,\n      \"notes\": \"Skill-only changes (markdown + worked examples).\",\n      \"tags\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"US-052\",\n      \"title\": \"LessonChat — sliding side panel UI scaffold + persisted draft in localStorage\",\n      \"description\": \"As a learner, I want a sliding side panel inside lessons where I can compose questions to an AI tutor and have my draft preserved across page reloads, so I can come back to a question without retyping.\",","numLines":280,"startLine":913,"totalLines":1307}}}
