{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TB4ZMBaVkq5TXR8eNQSEiL","type":"tool_result","content":"145\t  - **`accumulated` closure-variable pattern for streaming setState.** Rather than reading-then-writing React state in each token handler, keep a local `let accumulated = ''` in the async closure, increment it sync, and call `setMessages(prev => ...)` with a snapshot. Reading state inside an async callback would race against React's batched updates; the local var is the source of truth for \"what tokens have we received so far\" and gets passed to `finalizeStopped`/the post-loop terminal `setMessages` once.\n146\t  - **Typed `Connector` interface gotcha for `vi.spyOn` mocks.** Adding `chatStream` to `Connector` broke every existing spy that returned `{ name, chat }`. Test helper `fakeConnector(chatImpl, streamImpl?)` papers over this by defaulting `chatStream` to a single-token-then-done generator built from `chat`. Adopt a similar helper any time the Connector contract grows so the existing spies stay one-line.\n147\t  - **Don't put debug `console.log` near token streaming in playwright tests UNLESS you also ingest them in the test.** I added `[chat-debug]` lines in the component, then teaches the playwright `page.on('console')` listener to surface them — that's how I noticed the TypingDots-textContent bug (catch path ran with `accumulated.length=0` even though the bubble seemed to have 142 chars of content).\n148\t---\n149\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9bf3d4c0-be72-4235-a7a7-0162ef2f8d69","uuid":"e8e22b0c-d86c-4266-ae22-dd3b517a0816","timestamp":"2026-05-04T07:13:26.323Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/nukeemann/projects/ai_lecturer/.worktrees/US-056/scripts/ralph/progress.txt","content":"  - **`accumulated` closure-variable pattern for streaming setState.** Rather than reading-then-writing React state in each token handler, keep a local `let accumulated = ''` in the async closure, increment it sync, and call `setMessages(prev => ...)` with a snapshot. Reading state inside an async callback would race against React's batched updates; the local var is the source of truth for \"what tokens have we received so far\" and gets passed to `finalizeStopped`/the post-loop terminal `setMessages` once.\n  - **Typed `Connector` interface gotcha for `vi.spyOn` mocks.** Adding `chatStream` to `Connector` broke every existing spy that returned `{ name, chat }`. Test helper `fakeConnector(chatImpl, streamImpl?)` papers over this by defaulting `chatStream` to a single-token-then-done generator built from `chat`. Adopt a similar helper any time the Connector contract grows so the existing spies stay one-line.\n  - **Don't put debug `console.log` near token streaming in playwright tests UNLESS you also ingest them in the test.** I added `[chat-debug]` lines in the component, then teaches the playwright `page.on('console')` listener to surface them — that's how I noticed the TypingDots-textContent bug (catch path ran with `accumulated.length=0` even though the bubble seemed to have 142 chars of content).\n---\n","numLines":5,"startLine":145,"totalLines":149}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01RzdvzHsj895qAxnbBx8r6Y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018WqWZtLT4rVRDnuhQHPQhk","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/home/nukeemann/projects/ai_lecturer/.worktrees/US-056/scripts/ralph/progress.txt","old_string":"  - **Don't put debug `console.log` near token streaming in playwright tests UNLESS you also ingest them in the test.** I added `[chat-debug]` lines in the component, then teaches the playwright `page.on('console')` listener to surface them — that's how I noticed the TypingDots-textContent bug (catch path ran with `accumulated.length=0` even though the bubble seemed to have 142 chars of content).\n---","new_string":"  - **Don't put debug `console.log` near token streaming in playwright tests UNLESS you also ingest them in the test.** I added `[chat-debug]` lines in the component, then teaches the playwright `page.on('console')` listener to surface them — that's how I noticed the TypingDots-textContent bug (catch path ran with `accumulated.length=0` even though the bubble seemed to have 142 chars of content).\n---\n\n## 2026-05-04 - US-056\n- Authored `test-plan.md` at the repo root: end-to-end QA walkthrough that a maintainer can run in ≤30 min (experienced) / ≤60 min (new). Structure: §1 Setup → §2 Test Courses to Generate (3 distinct topics chosen to exercise different widget mixes — Course A \"Bubble sort algorithm\" Short/Beginner/Mostly-theory, Course B \"Linear regression for ML\" Standard/Some-experience/Balanced, Course C \"Computer vision: convolutions, edges, and Fourier transforms\" Comprehensive/Advanced/Mostly-practice) → §3 Walkthroughs (numbered checklist sections per area) → §4 Known limitations → §5 Sign-off.\n- Each test course entry lists topic prompt for Stage 1, exact refinement choices (level + duration chip + slider position with label), expected approximate module/lesson count tied to US-042's enum, and which widgets each course is expected to exercise.\n- Walkthrough sections (§3.1–§3.9) cover all the AC items: dashboard (empty + populated + Continue learning hero + search substring + slug-prefix + autocomplete) [US-014/019/036], wizard end-to-end Stages 1–5 [US-024/025/026/042], lesson layout + nav + TOC + prev/next + mark complete + auto-advance + j/k/⌘B/⌘. + Reset session [US-015/016/017/018/019/021/031], every widget type 14 sub-sections [US-007/008/010/011/012/013/030/038/039/043/044/045/046/047/048/049/050/051], LessonChat open + ask with section context + stop mid-stream + draft persistence + 503 fallback [US-052/053/054/055], theme toggle persistence [US-002/020], sources panel lesson + section [US-040/041], schemaVersion [US-037], logo navigates home [US-034], avatar dropdown [US-035].\n- Each item is a checkbox `- [ ]` with an explicit pass criterion (e.g. \"button morphs to **Submitted ✓**\", \"card badge shows **In progress · 1/N**\", \"**PNG appears within 10 s** of first matplotlib install\", \"italic suffix `— stopped by user` renders on its own line\", \"iframe src appends `?start=<sec>`\"). No vague \"works correctly\".\n- §4 Known Limitations lists 14 explicit out-of-MVP items: single-user, file-based not IndexedDB, course generation runs offline via ralph CLI not in-app, LessonChat needs Claude CLI, no cross-reload chat history, **PythonPlot (US-044) and Image (US-050) may not be wired in the registry** (per US-051 progress note: marked `passes: true` but code missing — the §3.4.8 PythonPlot and §3.4.14 Image sections include explicit \"verify with grep, mark N/A if absent\" instructions, so reviewers don't get stuck), Pyodide cooperative-interrupt impossible, in-memory wizard draft, search-index staleness on theory edit, widget-data search exclusion, no Polish accent-stripping, light-mode default, agent log out of scope, schemaVersion forward-compat only.\n- Files changed: test-plan.md (new — only file added; no code changes).\n- Quality: `npm run typecheck` clean (this is the only AC quality gate — `tests pass` and `lint passes` are not in the AC for US-056). No code touched, so no lint or test delta possible.\n- **Learnings for future iterations:**\n  - **Pure-documentation stories DO need to verify the story's specific quality gate, but only that one.** US-056's AC says \"Typecheck passes\" — not \"tests pass\", not \"lint clean\". Don't waste time on lint/test runs when the AC doesn't require them; just verify the one named gate. Same lesson as US-051 (skill-md-only stories).\n  - **`prd.json` lies about US-044 (PythonPlot) and US-050 (Image) — both marked `passes: true`, neither is actually in the registry or schema discriminated union.** Cross-checked: `src/widgets/registry.ts` `WidgetType` union has 13 types but excludes `pythonPlot` and `image`; `src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts` discriminated union likewise excludes them. The US-051 learning note flagged Image; PythonPlot has the same fate. Test plan needed to acknowledge this honestly without dropping the AC-mandated coverage — solution was to keep §3.4.8 / §3.4.14 sections complete with their pass criteria but front-load a **NOTE** at the bottom + a Known-Limitations item §4.6 with a one-line `grep` to verify.\n  - **Test plans should reference all the seed-test courses already in `/courses/`** — `pexp-test`, `cloze-test`, `dragmatch-test`, `datatable-test`, `video-test` cover the widgets that don't fit naturally into the seed `gauss-basics` course. Calling these out per-widget gives the reviewer a fast path even if they skip §2's \"Test Courses to Generate\" step (which requires a full ralph chain run).\n  - **Time-budget signal in the document.** AC says ≤30/≤60 min targets — the way I made this realistic was: (a) §2 explicitly tells reviewers they can skip course generation and use seeds (saves ~30 min × 3 courses), (b) §3 sections are ordered so the reviewer can do dashboard → wizard → seed-lesson nav → widgets → chat → theme → sources → schema → header in roughly that flow without backtracking, (c) widget §3.4 sub-sections are short enough (5–10 boxes each) that the whole §3.4 is ~10 minutes if no failures.\n  - **`courses/` already has six dedicated widget-test courses.** `ls courses/` showed cloze-test, datatable-test, dragmatch-test, gauss-basics, pexp-test, video-test — handy reference for any future story that needs a minimal repro lesson for a specific widget without spinning up the wizard.\n  - **The keyboard shortcut list in `src/components/ShortcutsModal.tsx` is the canonical source of truth** for what keys are wired. AC mentions j/k/⌘B/⌘. but ShortcutsModal.tsx also exposes Space (mark current section), n (next lesson), p (previous lesson), f (focus mode), and arrow keys ↑/↓ as aliases for k/j. Test plan covers j/k/⌘B/⌘. + Reset session per AC; the others aren't mandated so I didn't bloat the checklist.\n  - **Authoring tip: pick widget pass criteria from the original AC string.** Each `US-NNN` AC in `prd.json` has phrases like \"button morphs to **Stop** with `--danger` styling\", \"**Page X of Y** indicator centered below table\", \"italic suffix `— stopped by user` renders on its own line\". Quoting these verbatim in the checkbox items both (a) anchors the criterion to the originating story and (b) means a future reviewer can `git blame`/grep back to the spec source if a behavior changes.\n---"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":654,"cache_read_input_tokens":118489,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":654},"output_tokens":66,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9bf3d4c0-be72-4235-a7a7-0162ef2f8d69","uuid":"0a619c3d-2386-4a92-ac03-3b18172e7a3c"}
